oreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:00:42Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"test(browser): match source names exactly, not by partial match\n\nA card toggle is named for its source and its jump button is named\n\"Show <source>\", so any partial match resolved to both wherever the\nerror fixture put jump buttons on the page. Eleven locators matched\npartially; one went red as soon as the jump button started rendering a\ndisplay name instead of a raw slug, and two more had been asserting a\nlowercase slug that no longer exists and passing anyway, because string\nname matching ignores case.\n\nThe toggle assertion that proves an enable label is not absorbed into\nthe toggle''s name now counts the matches first, so a leaked label fails\non the assertion rather than on a locator that suddenly matches nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"ac24c28aa885b909493f30359251b3f58bf75d0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/ac24c28aa885b909493f30359251b3f58bf75d0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/a7ba8478ea368259f13d746816e3d6f3b05c6bea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/a7ba8478ea368259f13d746816e3d6f3b05c6bea","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKGE3YmE4NDc4ZWEzNjgyNTlmMTNkNzQ2ODE2ZTNkNmYzYjA1YzZiZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/ba755e4403412c06290e5aa74942eed11ee3ab72","sha":"ba755e4403412c06290e5aa74942eed11ee3ab72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/ba755e4403412c06290e5aa74942eed11ee3ab72"}],"sha":"a7ba8478ea368259f13d746816e3d6f3b05c6bea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/a7ba8478ea368259f13d746816e3d6f3b05c6bea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/ba755e4403412c06290e5aa74942eed11ee3ab72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T19:46:59Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T19:46:59Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"docs: prepare 0.17.0\n\nThe changelog entry covers what an operator will notice, built from the\ndiff rather than from descriptions, which caught five user-visible fixes\nthat no summary had mentioned.\n\nTwo factual errors in the released 0.16.0 entry are corrected rather\nthan restyled: the Babel 8 floor read \"Node 22.18 or newer\" when the\nreal range excludes Node 23 and Node 24.0 through 24.10, which told a\nreader on Node 24.5 they could build the panel when they cannot; and the\nstatus pills were described as each carrying a tone glyph, which is\nwrong for the neutral idle pill, which carries none.\n\nThe README described a control that does not exist, said the status\nsection was named something it is not, and its Node badge disagreed with\nthe prose beside it about whether Node 21 is supported. The security\npolicy still named a line two releases old. The theme selector moved to\nthe foot of the panel when the shared UI stopped resolving a placement\nthat had it leading a title-less shell, so the screenshot and the layout\ndescriptions follow it.\n\nThe screenshot of the USCG Light List note is re-encoded to about a\nthird of its size, which brings it under the App Store guidance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"688e4210cc5c4f04a005ed00c9786a1e9df89c37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/688e4210cc5c4f04a005ed00c9786a1e9df89c37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/ba755e4403412c06290e5aa74942eed11ee3ab72","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/ba755e4403412c06290e5aa74942eed11ee3ab72","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKGJhNzU1ZTQ0MDM0MTJjMDYyOTBlNWFhNzQ5NDJlZWQxMWVlM2FiNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/036a3f8c5b8572ed231f2ae59cafdb1078f79ba3","sha":"036a3f8c5b8572ed231f2ae59cafdb1078f79ba3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/036a3f8c5b8572ed231f2ae59cafdb1078f79ba3"}],"sha":"ba755e4403412c06290e5aa74942eed11ee3ab72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/ba755e4403412c06290e5aa74942eed11ee3ab72"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/036a3f8c5b8572ed231f2ae59cafdb1078f79ba3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T19:46:48Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T19:46:48Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(panel): validate Overpass endpoints, and adopt the shared UI contract\n\nBoth Overpass endpoint fields accepted anything, saved it, and were then\nsilently overridden: the plugin substituted its default for an unusable\nprimary and dropped bad mirror lines, so a typo persisted, was ignored,\nand vanished on the next mount while OpenSeaMap ran against an endpoint\nother than the one on screen. Both fields now validate against the same\nrule the plugin uses, rather than a second copy of it, and an invalid\nvalue blocks Save through the save bar''s own mechanism.\n\nThe collapsed Alerts header now states whether the proximity, route\ncorridor, and bridge air draft checks are armed, which the panel''s own\nsource cards already promised of a collapsed row.\n\nAn expired admin session read \"HTTP 401\" beside a promise that the next\npoll would retry, which it never could. It now says to sign in again,\nand keeps the retry note for failures a retry can recover.\n\nStatus labels read Healthy, Idle, Fetching, and Unreachable instead of\nrepeating the tone glyph''s own word, which had a screen reader announcing\n\"Success. ok\".\n\nA jump button beside an error for a source with no status row rendered\nthe internal slug. On an imperial server a whole-number length field\nshowed a fractional floor a numeric keypad could not reach. Clearing the\nmirror list left the panel permanently dirty and saved a one-element\nlist holding an empty string.\n\nThe recent-error banner hands focus to the status section when it goes,\nso a poll reporting no errors under a focused jump button no longer\ndrops the reader on the body. The accessibility sweep now opens a source\ncard, its Advanced disclosure, and Alerts rather than auditing only the\nlanding state, and the fallback list no longer autocapitalizes or\nspell-checks a URL typed on a helm tablet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"80d3ecae4638447c5301cdc71bfedd273e642c62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/80d3ecae4638447c5301cdc71bfedd273e642c62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/036a3f8c5b8572ed231f2ae59cafdb1078f79ba3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/036a3f8c5b8572ed231f2ae59cafdb1078f79ba3","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDAzNmEzZjhjNWI4NTcyZWQyMzFmMmFlNTljYWZkYjEwNzhmNzliYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/2ebf75b4a7bbe45c15b4b6fc3f2f44264392c9ab","sha":"2ebf75b4a7bbe45c15b4b6fc3f2f44264392c9ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/2ebf75b4a7bbe45c15b4b6fc3f2f44264392c9ab"}],"sha":"036a3f8c5b8572ed231f2ae59cafdb1078f79ba3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/036a3f8c5b8572ed231f2ae59cafdb1078f79ba3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/2ebf75b4a7bbe45c15b4b6fc3f2f44264392c9ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T19:46:34Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T19:46:34Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(plugin): six defects in scanning, teardown, dedupe, and note detail\n\nA cleared-route delta republished while no route was cached forced a\nscan that bypasses both the movement and the interval gates, costing one\nlist request to every enabled upstream per delta. The clear path now\ndelegates to the same commit function the refresh path uses, so one\nplace owns the notify-only-on-change rule.\n\nA throw while wiring the position monitor stranded its navigation\nsubscription with no handle, and every restart stacked another live\nhandler. The subscription is now acquired last, after the wiring and the\nlogging, so there is nothing to unwind rather than an unwind to get\nright.\n\nDuplicate points of interest were missed toward the poles because the\ncell grid projected longitude through the mean latitude of the list. Two\nmarinas 49 m apart at latitude 75 landed two cells apart once an\nequatorial point pulled the mean to 50. The reference is now the\npoleward-most latitude in the set.\n\nA note resource path of __proto__ or constructor answered with a\nbuilt-in instead of a 404.\n\nA navigation aid with no readable light characteristic rendered an empty\n\"Light:\" line, and gave a structured client a blank Character row beside\nit. Emptiness now comes off the rendered value rather than off which\nfields are present, so the two renderings cannot disagree. An aid still\ncarrying a usable range or focal plane keeps those.\n\nOpenSeaMap note detail labels a seamark''s color with the American\nspelling, which a client matching that label string will see.\n\nTwo comments asserted counts the code owns, one of which had already\nmisled a document: both now point at the callers instead.\n\nEach fix carries a test verified to fail on the code it replaces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"35ccc3f9fc48d88b6ae63a56e66e7d5f1ae22327","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/35ccc3f9fc48d88b6ae63a56e66e7d5f1ae22327"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/2ebf75b4a7bbe45c15b4b6fc3f2f44264392c9ab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/2ebf75b4a7bbe45c15b4b6fc3f2f44264392c9ab","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDJlYmY3NWI0YTdiYmU0NWMxNWI0YjZmYzNmMmY0NDI2NDM5MmM5YWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/6f5563f443998e4dc932f76982a9872d638f1c1a","sha":"6f5563f443998e4dc932f76982a9872d638f1c1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/6f5563f443998e4dc932f76982a9872d638f1c1a"}],"sha":"2ebf75b4a7bbe45c15b4b6fc3f2f44264392c9ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/2ebf75b4a7bbe45c15b4b6fc3f2f44264392c9ab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/6f5563f443998e4dc932f76982a9872d638f1c1a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T19:46:19Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T19:46:19Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"build: bring dependencies current and harden the packaging gate\n\nNine packages move, including react and react-dom to 19.3.0 and\n@signalk/server-api to 2.32.0. The shared UI pin goes to 0.10.1, which\ninstalls tab styles with Tabs rather than with every panel.\n\nTwo holds stay, both still enforced: @types/node tracks the lowest\nsupported engines.node major, checked by scripts/check-package.mjs, and\neslint stays on 9.x while eslint-plugin-react and neostandard both\ndeclare an eslint ^9 peer.\n\ncheck:panel now renders the built remote the way the Signal K Admin host\ndoes, asserting the production JSX runtime and the panel''s own content\nrather than only its files. The packaging gate rejects prepare,\npostinstall, and preinstall lifecycle scripts, which npm 10 executes\nduring a pack that asks it not to.\n\nSix action pin comments named the wrong release, setup-go was a major\nbehind, and plugin-ci cited a registry host that no longer exists. The\nreusable plugin-ci pin moves to a revision that adds a blocking async\ncrash trap to the lifecycle check.\n\nwebpack.config.cjs records why this panel deliberately does not require\nthe Admin dependency inventory: it is a peer validator that exits on any\nmissing peer, its React range is wider than the shared UI requires, and\nit lags the Admin it describes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"b93a3fcff8c75d9fbc0f86b1e36111dbafd96ecd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/b93a3fcff8c75d9fbc0f86b1e36111dbafd96ecd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/6f5563f443998e4dc932f76982a9872d638f1c1a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/6f5563f443998e4dc932f76982a9872d638f1c1a","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDZmNTU2M2Y0NDM5OThlNGRjOTMyZjc2OTgyYTk4NzJkNjM4ZjFjMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/9942c8974d2d70bff487d2b20b2abc838f9ec76f","sha":"9942c8974d2d70bff487d2b20b2abc838f9ec76f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/9942c8974d2d70bff487d2b20b2abc838f9ec76f"}],"sha":"6f5563f443998e4dc932f76982a9872d638f1c1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/6f5563f443998e4dc932f76982a9872d638f1c1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/9942c8974d2d70bff487d2b20b2abc838f9ec76f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T21:50:17Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T21:50:17Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"chore: prepare 0.16.0\n\nVersion, release notes, and the documentation this work made wrong.\n\nThe security policy described a feature removed in 0.12.0, including an\nOpenRouter API key it said the plugin stores and vessel positions it said the\nplugin transmits. It does neither. It also listed four upstream services when\nthere are eight. CODEOWNERS still named the owner of the project this one was\nforked from, so every pull request since the fork has requested review from\nsomeone unconnected to it.\n\nThree of the four status-pill labels were wrong, the per-source detail was\ndescribed as a hover tooltip when it is visible text in the expanded card, and\nthe Alerts section was documented as opening itself when an alarm is enabled,\nwhich it has never done.\n\nRemoved: a vector-tile test fixture orphaned when that feature went in 0.12.0\nand the gitattributes line that existed only for it, two icon sizes below the\nApp Store''s minimum that nothing referenced, two npm scripts nothing invoked,\nand lint and type-check entries excluding a directory that has never existed\nin this repository. `watch:panel` stays but now runs through the panel build\nscript, so it prints the Node floor notice rather than a raw engine error.\n\nThe full-tree dependency audit no longer gates a release. It covers the\ndevelopment toolchain, where an advisory carries no runtime exposure for an\noperator and sometimes has no upstream fix to take, so it now reports from its\nown CI job. The runtime audit, which is what the plugin registry scores, still\nblocks and is clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"5b0427c785b701feec73efb732276aa5e7728646","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/5b0427c785b701feec73efb732276aa5e7728646"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/9942c8974d2d70bff487d2b20b2abc838f9ec76f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/9942c8974d2d70bff487d2b20b2abc838f9ec76f","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDk5NDJjODk3NGQyZDcwYmZmNDg3ZDJiMjBiMmFiYzgzOGY5ZWM3NmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/bd51e096629a3e92a26861da6749f19c7677414b","sha":"bd51e096629a3e92a26861da6749f19c7677414b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/bd51e096629a3e92a26861da6749f19c7677414b"}],"sha":"9942c8974d2d70bff487d2b20b2abc838f9ec76f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/9942c8974d2d70bff487d2b20b2abc838f9ec76f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/bd51e096629a3e92a26861da6749f19c7677414b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T21:50:03Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T21:50:03Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"feat(panel): rebuild on the shared component library, and fix two dead paths\n\nThe configuration panel is built on signalk-nearlcrews-ui 0.9.0 throughout: a\nshared shell, save bar, fields, collapsibles, and text in place of the local\ncopies it carried. The panel now ships no CSS of its own.\n\nTwo consumer-owned behaviours were broken independently of that work. A\nstatus-poll failure was announced through a live region created in the same\ncommit as its message, which is not read aloud reliably; the region is now\nalways present and only its text changes. And the \"Show <source>\" button in\nthe error list did nothing while the Data sources section was collapsed, and\nnever moved focus, so it was a pointer-and-sighted-only shortcut. It now opens\nthe section, scrolls to the card, and puts focus on that card''s own toggle,\nwhose accessible name is the source and which is where the section returns\nfocus when collapsed, so the destination is announced rather than only shown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"bd940113cf7ef5a5518a07cc2162ab14b1c48508","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/bd940113cf7ef5a5518a07cc2162ab14b1c48508"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/bd51e096629a3e92a26861da6749f19c7677414b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/bd51e096629a3e92a26861da6749f19c7677414b","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKGJkNTFlMDk2NjI5YTNlOTJhMjY4NjFkYTY3NDlmMTljNzY3NzQxNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/004255e9305a0ff4a7bcad4b17523adea64c0593","sha":"004255e9305a0ff4a7bcad4b17523adea64c0593","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/004255e9305a0ff4a7bcad4b17523adea64c0593"}],"sha":"bd51e096629a3e92a26861da6749f19c7677414b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/bd51e096629a3e92a26861da6749f19c7677414b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/004255e9305a0ff4a7bcad4b17523adea64c0593/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T21:49:54Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T21:49:54Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix: stop a misshapen upstream response emptying a source in silence\n\nA response that parsed as valid JSON but carried an unexpected shape emptied\nthe stored records for its source and reported a successful fetch. A renamed\nfield in the USCG Light List, the Local Notice to Mariners, the NOAA CO-OPS\nstation list, or the NGA World Port Index would have removed everything that\nsource had stored, on one refresh, with the panel still green. The Local\nNotice layers carry the hazard markers the proximity and route alarms run on,\nso the alarms would have gone quiet.\n\nA network fault was already handled: an error page throws in JSON.parse and is\nrecorded. This was the well-formed body in the wrong shape, which is what an\nupstream field rename looks like.\n\nA collection that is missing or is not an array is now an error, and a page\ncarrying rows that parse to nothing is a failure rather than an empty result.\nNeither advances the stored cache validators, so the next refresh re-fetches\nrather than being told nothing changed, which is what would otherwise have\nmade the loss stick. A genuinely empty page is still representable, because a\nsource that really does retire its rows must stay expressible.\n\nDownloads now negotiate compression, which the one-shot transport never\nrequested. The World Port Index refresh drops from 6.3 MB to about 579 KB, the\nUSACE dams query from 1.4 MB to 74 KB, and the CO-OPS station list from 777 KB\nto 32 KB. The response cap counts decompressed bytes, so a small compressed\nbody that expands past it is still refused.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"643f874d0a64e484af86945252ae81c4e45d4c83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/643f874d0a64e484af86945252ae81c4e45d4c83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/004255e9305a0ff4a7bcad4b17523adea64c0593","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/004255e9305a0ff4a7bcad4b17523adea64c0593","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDAwNDI1NWU5MzA1YTBmZjRhN2JjYWQ0YjE3NTIzYWRlYTY0YzA1OTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/4737f1e1fc17157733aee5b258daa1a963af2119","sha":"4737f1e1fc17157733aee5b258daa1a963af2119","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/4737f1e1fc17157733aee5b258daa1a963af2119"}],"sha":"004255e9305a0ff4a7bcad4b17523adea64c0593","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/004255e9305a0ff4a7bcad4b17523adea64c0593"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/4737f1e1fc17157733aee5b258daa1a963af2119/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T21:49:42Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T21:49:42Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix: warn about hazards the alarm path could previously miss\n\nThree ways an alarm could fail to warn, none of which announced itself.\n\nA hazard could pass inside the alarm radius without an alarm at all. Alarms\nwere evaluated once a minute and every 100 metres of movement, a cadence\nunrelated to the radius the operator configured, while the distance covered\nbetween evaluations can exceed the along-track length of the alarm zone. At\nthe default 500 metre radius a hazard 450 metres abeam is missed from 20\nknots, and one dead ahead from about 32. The data was already fetched; it was\nnever examined while the hazard was inside the radius. Alarm checks now run\nagainst the last list on every position fix, sampled from the tightest\nconfigured radius, so no extra upstream requests are made. A radius too small\nto honour at any plausible speed is reported at startup, and a pass that\noutruns the sampling is reported when it happens.\n\nA slow upstream cleared a standing alarm and re-raised it with sound once the\nsource answered. The outputs read each tick''s combined list as proof of what\nexists, so a source that timed out, failed beside a successful one, or served\na partial layer took its hazards with it. A tracked hazard is now held at the\nposition it was last reported at and clears on the same geometry as any\nother, or after thirty minutes unreported, with a message that says so rather\nthan claiming the vessel has moved clear.\n\nAn unresolvable bridge is asked about once a minute rather than once per\nevaluation, so moving evaluation onto the fix rate does not multiply requests\nto a third-party service. Failures are held in their own map, never in the\nclearance cache, so a failed fetch cannot be read back as an authoritative\nabsence of clearance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"5053d1c311a82f348cf473c7a6ff4ea8afe8ef0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/5053d1c311a82f348cf473c7a6ff4ea8afe8ef0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/4737f1e1fc17157733aee5b258daa1a963af2119","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/4737f1e1fc17157733aee5b258daa1a963af2119","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDQ3MzdmMWUxZmMxNzE1NzczM2FlZTViMjU4ZGFhMWE5NjNhZjIxMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/f6649b131e1df05bd6bdc0e855f95f34a91dc39e","sha":"f6649b131e1df05bd6bdc0e855f95f34a91dc39e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/f6649b131e1df05bd6bdc0e855f95f34a91dc39e"}],"sha":"4737f1e1fc17157733aee5b258daa1a963af2119","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/4737f1e1fc17157733aee5b258daa1a963af2119"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.git