.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"docs: complete the 0.15.6 changelog and refresh the release docs\n\nThe 0.15.6 entry omitted five shipped fixes: the card-header and\nrecent-error touch targets, the one-sided USCG LNM effective date, the\ncourse-reader and clearance-resolver teardown, and the README screenshot\nanchors. Each gains a Fixed bullet, and the entry date moves to the\npublish date.\n\nThe README highlights gain the touch-target work, and the release doc''s\nengines line catches up to the published range.","tree":{"sha":"b99a26357888154bdddfc80e800c2ce0cc98539f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/b99a26357888154bdddfc80e800c2ce0cc98539f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/754a33a23a511536d16058e7ba3a6abdda4a0198","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/754a33a23a511536d16058e7ba3a6abdda4a0198","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDc1NGEzM2EyM2E1MTE1MzZkMTYwNThlN2JhM2E2YWJkZGE0YTAxOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/0bc74a0c491dbeb5ecc9c43a2898eb318e876c48","sha":"0bc74a0c491dbeb5ecc9c43a2898eb318e876c48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/0bc74a0c491dbeb5ecc9c43a2898eb318e876c48"}],"sha":"754a33a23a511536d16058e7ba3a6abdda4a0198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/754a33a23a511536d16058e7ba3a6abdda4a0198"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/0bc74a0c491dbeb5ecc9c43a2898eb318e876c48/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:43:08Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:43:08Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"test: close the pin-guard repair hole and stop reusing a fixture server\n\nThe shared UI pin was guarded by a single equality check in the packaging\nscript and again in the browser spec, which leaves a repair path that quietly\nweakens it. After npm install signalk-nearlcrews-ui@latest rewrites the pin to\na range such as ^0.9.0, the obvious repair is to paste the failing value into\nthe expected-version literal. Both sides then agree on ^0.9.0, the check\npasses, and its message still claims the pin is exact, so the guard reports\nsuccess while the exactness it exists to defend is gone.\n\nEach site now asserts two things. A shape assertion requires an exact version\nand is never hand-edited, so it keeps holding whatever the literal is bumped\nto, and the literal stays as the deliberate-bump tripwire. Both report the\nvalue they received rather than only the value they wanted, so a failure names\nthe range that caused it. The shape carries a leading 0 on purpose: the shared\nUI is 0.x, where its own guidance is to pin exactly because the API may change\nbetween minors, so a 1.0 release is meant to trip this and be looked at.\n\nVerified discriminating at both sites rather than by reading. With the pin\ntemporarily set to ^0.8.2, the packaging script fails with the received value\nquoted and the browser spec throws before any test runs; restoring 0.8.2 makes\nboth pass. The regex accepts 0.8.2 and rejects ^0.8.2, ~0.8.2, 0.8.2-rc.1,\n>=0.8.2, 0.8.x, and a bare wildcard.\n\nThe Playwright fixture server also no longer reuses a server this run did not\nstart. It was reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI, which is true off CI, so a\nstale server left by an earlier run could serve a suite measuring something\nother than the build that just ran. Port 4177 is unique among the sibling\npanels and the fixture already sets strictPort, so this closes the last way a\nsuite could quietly measure the wrong panel. Failing to bind is the honest\noutcome.","tree":{"sha":"cc6da13e28be1fdf796982b05125e4469b75e47b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/cc6da13e28be1fdf796982b05125e4469b75e47b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/0bc74a0c491dbeb5ecc9c43a2898eb318e876c48","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/0bc74a0c491dbeb5ecc9c43a2898eb318e876c48","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDBiYzc0YTBjNDkxZGJlYjVlY2M5YzQzYTI4OThlYjMxOGU4NzZjNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/34f48e5d6368087fb14bc5ac0e6716afb4665edb","sha":"34f48e5d6368087fb14bc5ac0e6716afb4665edb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/34f48e5d6368087fb14bc5ac0e6716afb4665edb"}],"sha":"0bc74a0c491dbeb5ecc9c43a2898eb318e876c48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/0bc74a0c491dbeb5ecc9c43a2898eb318e876c48"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/34f48e5d6368087fb14bc5ac0e6716afb4665edb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:34:55Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:34:55Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"test: give the coarse-pointer sweep its own timeout budget\n\nThe sweep expands every collapsible section, then checks every toggle so the\ngated fields render as live controls, which is roughly eighty interactions\nbefore it measures anything. That is deliberate, since the two undersized\ntargets this panel shipped were both found by measuring everything rather\nthan by inspecting a list of suspects, but it makes this the longest test in\nthe repository by a wide margin: about 26 seconds on an idle host and over 40\non a busy one, against a 30-second project default.\n\nThe test now sets its own 120-second budget instead of the project default\nrising for all eight. Measured discriminating: with the project timeout\nforced to 20 seconds the sweep still passes in 26.8 seconds, which is only\nreachable through the per-test budget.\n\nThe budget covers the test body, not the shared beforeEach, because the hook\nruns before the body can raise the limit. That split is correct here: page\nsetup finishing inside the normal default is itself worth enforcing, and only\nthe measuring pass needs the extra room.","tree":{"sha":"471b2d47f9567b75b9dd364231e7a3503b8c25a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/471b2d47f9567b75b9dd364231e7a3503b8c25a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/34f48e5d6368087fb14bc5ac0e6716afb4665edb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/34f48e5d6368087fb14bc5ac0e6716afb4665edb","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDM0ZjQ4ZTVkNjM2ODA4N2ZiMTRiYzVhYzBlNjcxNmFmYjQ2NjVlZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/4beae840f4c6f50ac56d163f0c07ea6370b402d2","sha":"4beae840f4c6f50ac56d163f0c07ea6370b402d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/4beae840f4c6f50ac56d163f0c07ea6370b402d2"}],"sha":"34f48e5d6368087fb14bc5ac0e6716afb4665edb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/34f48e5d6368087fb14bc5ac0e6716afb4665edb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/4beae840f4c6f50ac56d163f0c07ea6370b402d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:23:17Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:23:17Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"chore: update shared UI to 0.8.2\n\nThe panel''s sticky footer bar now reaches its final geometry inside the frame\nthe triggering event scheduled, and its docking decision carries a hysteresis\nband, so geometry landing on the threshold keeps the state it has instead of\nalternating between docked and natural flow. A pointer press that moves focus\nno longer produces a clearance scroll at all, so a press on a control the bar\noverlaps lands on that control rather than on whatever the scroll moved under\nthe pointer. Keyboard and programmatic focus still clear a covered control\nimmediately.\n\nThe release also gives compact and icon-only buttons a minimum width from the\ncontrol size token, and re-reads the shared theme in a panel revealed inside a\nretained CollapsibleSection. Neither reaches this panel: its footer buttons\ncarry text at the default size, and it mounts one PanelRoot at the root rather\nthan one per section. The 0.15.6 entry therefore claims only the action bar\nbehavior.\n\nThe pinned version is named in the packaging gate, the browser suite, the\ntoolchain notes, the README, and the generated notices, so all of them move\ntogether.","tree":{"sha":"ecbe9fa2c5f15fdc44face939672c1e0f135d800","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/ecbe9fa2c5f15fdc44face939672c1e0f135d800"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/4beae840f4c6f50ac56d163f0c07ea6370b402d2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https:/