r}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/443825c5148b30347a8f6ba142def468e8a3ffaf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:22:56Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:22:56Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(stores): prune disabled CO-OPS families and sweep orphaned Light List pages\n\nTwo small store-hygiene gaps: records of a CO-OPS station family the\nuser turned off never served but inflated the record count (which feeds\nthe recorded fetch size and the panel''s cache size) and were rewritten\nto disk forever; the refresh now prunes them, and the both-families-off\nbranch flushes the prune before its skip return. And a Light List page\nfile orphaned by a crash between the page write and the metadata write\nwas unreachable by pruneDistricts, which walks metadata keys; load now\nsweeps unreferenced page files best-effort, one readdir per cold start.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1fdaaf06c8e6394fc032d91819788bd64d507046","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/1fdaaf06c8e6394fc032d91819788bd64d507046"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/443825c5148b30347a8f6ba142def468e8a3ffaf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/443825c5148b30347a8f6ba142def468e8a3ffaf","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDQ0MzgyNWM1MTQ4YjMwMzQ3YThmNmJhMTQyZGVmNDY4ZThhM2ZmYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/392d2ff9b13ac4c4ea4da9478636d0dcd145d20b","sha":"392d2ff9b13ac4c4ea4da9478636d0dcd145d20b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/392d2ff9b13ac4c4ea4da9478636d0dcd145d20b"}],"sha":"443825c5148b30347a8f6ba142def468e8a3ffaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/443825c5148b30347a8f6ba142def468e8a3ffaf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/392d2ff9b13ac4c4ea4da9478636d0dcd145d20b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:19:27Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:19:27Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(status): honest recording around failures and outages\n\nEight recording gaps let the status read better (or noisier) than\nreality:\n\n- A WPI detail miss inside the freshness window ran the recorded\n  detail wrapper over a no-op refresh, repainting the pill green during\n  an outage. Both quiet branches (freshness window and failure\n  cool-down) now skip the wrapper.\n- A list result landing after the registry''s five-second race was never\n  recorded, so a source whose markers were on the chart kept showing the\n  transient \"waiting\" skip for a whole debounce window. A late fresh\n  result now records its list fetch.\n- The Light List and LNM refreshes recorded one error per failed page,\n  so a single NAVCEN outage filled the whole capped recent-errors list\n  and hid every other source. Each pass now records one aggregated\n  error, and an empty catalog can no longer record a vacuous reachable\n  fetch.\n- The bulk sources stamped the whole on-disk index size as the fetch\n  count, so an all-304 pass reported tens of thousands of \"fetched\"\n  records. The count now reports what the pass actually ingested.\n- The ActiveCaptain source escalated a transient per-POI detail failure\n  to setPluginError, bypassing the start-error latch every peer source\n  respects. It now records onto the per-source status only.\n- A CO-OPS install with both station families off sat on a bare idle\n  pill; it now records why it is skipping and tags its list as skipped.\n- A stale offline serve left the server-wide plugin line reading as a\n  normal green status through an outage of any length. The notes output\n  now appends \"N sources offline, showing cached data\", backed by a\n  cheap unreachableSources reader on the status recorder.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"339e601c9c06dd520a8d1aff6363dc2bd97632d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/339e601c9c06dd520a8d1aff6363dc2bd97632d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/392d2ff9b13ac4c4ea4da9478636d0dcd145d20b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/392d2ff9b13ac4c4ea4da9478636d0dcd145d20b","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDM5MmQyZmY5YjEzYWM0YzRlYTRkYTk0Nzg2MzZkMGRjZDE0NWQyMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/d10afe215a85d5e3251712d4a723415dfb37ba31","sha":"d10afe215a85d5e3251712d4a723415dfb37ba31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/d10afe215a85d5e3251712d4a723415dfb37ba31"}],"sha":"392d2ff9b13ac4c4ea4da9478636d0dcd145d20b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/392d2ff9b13ac4c4ea4da9478636d0dcd145d20b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/d10afe215a85d5e3251712d4a723415dfb37ba31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:12:45Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:12:45Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(arcgis): verify pinned layer identity once per session\n\nThe NOAA ENC layer ids and the USACE query URLs are pinned, and both\ncan drift silently: a service republish renumbers layer ids (or, for\nthe ArcGIS Online locks service, changes the org item id) while the\nstale reference still answers 200, so another layer''s features would be\nlabeled as wrecks, obstructions, rocks, locks, or dams and fed to the\nalarms with nothing recording the mislabel. Each client now fetches the\nlayer metadata once per session before the first query and matches the\nlayer name against its kind pattern; a definite mismatch fails that\nlayer''s queries loudly (and stays failed for the session), while an\nunreachable metadata endpoint fails open, since an unreachable service\nalready fails the query itself.\n\nLive names probed 2026-07-27: Coastal.Wreck_point,\nCoastal.Obstruction_point, Coastal.Underwater_Awash_Rock_point (with\nband-specific prefixes), Lock, and National Inventory of Dams.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ad66850e21149277f8a7e09bc09b0c6f8d189d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/8ad66850e21149277f8a7e09bc09b0c6f8d189d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/d10afe215a85d5e3251712d4a723415dfb37ba31","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/d10afe215a85d5e3251712d4a723415dfb37ba31","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKGQxMGFmZTIxNWE4NWQ1ZTMyNTE3MTJkNGE3MjM0MTVkZmIzN2JhMzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/27a2cd2c451142be7eacc22be016a88d7cf03c10","sha":"27a2cd2c451142be7eacc22be016a88d7cf03c10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/27a2cd2c451142be7eacc22be016a88d7cf03c10"}],"sha":"d10afe215a85d5e3251712d4a723415dfb37ba31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/d10afe215a85d5e3251712d4a723415dfb37ba31"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/27a2cd2c451142be7eacc22be016a88d7cf03c10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:06:15Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:06:15Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(uscg-lnm): prune retired catalog files and correct the catalog notes\n\nThe LNM store had no prune: a file whose key left the pinned catalog\nsurvived load, kept serving from the union, and for the Hazard-typed\ndanger layers kept arming the proximity and route-corridor alarms\nforever. The refresh now prunes store files against the pinned catalog\nbefore each pass, mirroring the Light List''s pruneDistricts.\n\nA live probe also refuted two documented claims: the MSI host answers\n404 one page past each category''s end (the stated reason for pinning\nsaid it answered 200, discouraging the exact probe that catches\ndrift), and the multi-page categories overlap heavily rather than\nduplicating byte-identically. The catalog notes now record the probed\nreality, the union iterates file keys in sorted order so the winner for\na shared id is deterministic, and the catalog test asserts the\nper-layer page arrays rather than only the flattened total.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c731a6a1ed08cbff68dfbaa4134f7326db6215f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/c731a6a1ed08cbff68dfbaa4134f7326db6215f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/27a2cd2c451142be7eacc22be016a88d7cf03c10","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/27a2cd2c451142be7eacc22be016a88d7cf03c10","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDI3YTJjZDJjNDUxMTQyYmU3ZWFjYzIyYmUwMTZhODhkN2NmMDNjMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/dfb17e48a255f57b218b5cdf427de28ce70511e6","sha":"dfb17e48a255f57b218b5cdf427de28ce70511e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/dfb17e48a255f57b218b5cdf427de28ce70511e6"}],"sha":"27a2cd2c451142be7eacc22be016a88d7cf03c10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/27a2cd2c451142be7eacc22be016a88d7cf03c10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/dfb17e48a255f57b218b5cdf427de28ce70511e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:03:15Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:03:15Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(http): cap the request-queue depth and bound the Overpass failover chain\n\nThe queued client bounded every resource except one: the waiting list\ngrew without limit when polls arrived faster than the throttle drained,\nwhich is exactly the state a cache-disabled source in front of a slow\nupstream produces. The queue now caps its depth and rejects the oldest\nwaiter on overflow, since the newest request reflects the current\nviewport while the oldest has likely been abandoned already.\n\nSeparately, the Overpass failover chain multiplied bounds that are each\ncorrect in isolation: three mirrors times a full per-endpoint retry,\nbackoff, and Retry-After budget could hold one of the two queue slots\nfor minutes. The chain now carries a ninety-second wall-clock budget;\nonce spent, the last error propagates instead of starting another\nmirror.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"38477367547fce1420800fe1c396d8ad86fcdd73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/38477367547fce1420800fe1c396d8ad86fcdd73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/dfb17e48a255f57b218b5cdf427de28ce70511e6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/dfb17e48a255f57b218b5cdf427de28ce70511e6","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKGRmYjE3ZTQ4YTI1NWY1N2IyMThiNWNkZjQyN2RlMjhjZTcwNTExZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/e754fc45a4d10775afcc0556377afb8f7bf10557","sha":"e754fc45a4d10775afcc0556377afb8f7bf10557","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/e754fc45a4d10775afcc0556377afb8f7bf10557"}],"sha":"dfb17e48a255f57b218b5cdf427de28ce70511e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/dfb17e48a255f57b218b5cdf427de28ce70511e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/e754fc45a4d10775afcc0556377afb8f7bf10557/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T18:53:16Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T18:53:16Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(route-hazard): force a scan only when the active route actually changes\n\nEvery committed course refresh called onRouteChange unconditionally, and\nthat reaches a forced scan that bypasses both the position monitor''s\none-minute interval gate and its 100 m movement gate. The Course API\nemits nextPoint.position only on a genuine destination change, but the\nsame path carries re-publications from external NMEA course sources,\nwhich repeat an unchanged destination continuously, so an\nautopilot-driven vessel ran a throttle-free list fan-out per delta. The\nreader now compares the resolved route (id and waypoints ahead) against\nthe cached one and forces a scan only on a real change, which also\nrestores the bound a bridge-clearance-resolver comment wrongly claimed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f46fa9cb8ca87b4a1a93839de6cbe9047a97e178","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/f46fa9cb8ca87b4a1a93839de6cbe9047a97e178"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/e754fc45a4d10775afcc0556377afb8f7bf10557","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/e754fc45a4d10775afcc0556377afb8f7bf10557","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKGU3NTRmYzQ1YTRkMTA3NzVhZmNjMDU1NjM3N2FmYjhmN2JmMTA1NTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/79ed9e879ca210655e3e482306534cedcf75463c","sha":"79ed9e879ca210655e3e482306534cedcf75463c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/79ed9e879ca210655e3e482306534cedcf75463c"}],"sha":"e754fc45a4d10775afcc0556377afb8f7bf10557","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/e754fc45a4d10775afcc0556377afb8f7bf10557"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/79ed9e879ca210655e3e482306534cedcf75463c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T18:51:30Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T18:51:30Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(bbox-debounce): failure cool-down, degraded retention, and single-flight without the cache\n\nFour related gaps let a failing upstream be re-queried on every\nchartplotter poll instead of on a bounded cadence:\n\n- A failed cold fetch evicted its entry, so every poll re-launched the\n  request. The entry is now retained with a failure stamp; reads inside\n  a one-minute cool-down replay the rejection without touching the\n  network (the offline fallback still engages) and the first read after\n  it retries.\n- A failed background revalidation left the entry stale with nothing\n  remembered, so the next poll revalidated again, back to back against a\n  dead upstream. The same cool-down now spaces revalidations.\n- A shouldCache veto deleted the entry, at both the cold and the\n  revalidation site, so one failing NOAA ENC layer re-fanned-out every\n  enabled layer on every poll and the revalidation-site veto even\n  destroyed warm entries, turning non-blocking serves into blocking cold\n  misses. A vetoed value is now retained as degraded with its freshness\n  shortened to one minute, so the failed layer retries through\n  background revalidation while the healthy layers keep serving.\n- Disabling the cache (refresh window 0) also disabled the in-flight\n  collapse, so a request slower than the registry''s five-second window\n  was re-launched and its result discarded on every poll, and the source\n  never delivered a list. Concurrent identical requests now share one\n  in-flight fetch even with the cache off, dropped as soon as it\n  settles, so no settled result is ever reused.\n\nFailed neighbor prefetches ride the same retention: the peek guard now\nsuppresses re-prefetching a broken tile during its cool-down.\n\nThe ArcGIS factory wires the revalidation-error hook the OpenSeaMap and\nActiveCaptain sources already had, so a NOAA ENC or USACE outage behind\na warm tile is recorded instead of staying invisible, and it accepts an\ninjectable clock so the tests can cross the new windows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"20f5763753c10b5d5b9d329b3d4a33b174b27c12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/20f5763753c10b5d5b9d329b3d4a33b174b27c12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/79ed9e879ca210655e3e482306534cedcf75463c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/79ed9e879ca210655e3e482306534cedcf75463c","node_id":"C_kwDOSkbgHdoAKDc5ZWQ5ZTg3OWNhMjEwNjU1ZTNlNDgyMzA2NTM0Y2VkY2Y3NTQ2M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commit/b8b439e60db2ce0c21d6381dde564e2596fdac8f","sha":"b8b439e60db2ce0c21d6381dde564e2596fdac8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/b8b439e60db2ce0c21d6381dde564e2596fdac8f"}],"sha":"79ed9e879ca210655e3e482306534cedcf75463c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/79ed9e879ca210655e3e482306534cedcf75463c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/commits/b8b439e60db2ce0c21d6381dde564e2596fdac8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T18:30:02Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T18:30:02Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(uscg-light-list): track NAVCEN''s District 8 contraction and prune retired pages\n\nNAVCEN consolidated District 8 from eleven light-list pages to ten (a\ndirect probe confirms lightListD08_11.geojson now answers 404 while\npages 1 through 10 and every other district''s pinned coverage still\nanswer 200), so every refresh pass logged an HTTP 404 for the retired\npage. Drop the pair from the pinned table, and teach the refresh to\nprune store pages that leave the table: a retired page''s aids are\nremoved from memory immediately and from metadata and disk on the next\nflush, instead of serving forever. The page files are deleted only after\nthe metadata that stops referencing them commits, so a crash in between\nleaves nothing the loader would read.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea1b2bb289f2e4d0e87e0a291df29fd846d56b51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/trees/ea1b2bb289f2e4d0e87e0a291df29fd846d56b51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-crows-nest/git/commits/b8b439e60db2ce0c21d6381dde564e2596fdac8f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://