erified_at":"2026-07-27T13:17:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/b7dd784525547ad178e11c94ff47d2d6322848f6","node_id":"C_kwDOSkir09oAKGI3ZGQ3ODQ1MjU1NDdhZDE3OGUxMWM5NGZmNDdkMmQ2MzIyODQ4ZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/54ca5f0143cdce1e48f8163874ee41c036ca1c7f","sha":"54ca5f0143cdce1e48f8163874ee41c036ca1c7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/54ca5f0143cdce1e48f8163874ee41c036ca1c7f"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/12a64c63cffd5c6be324756aea3f1f2e0808eea3","sha":"12a64c63cffd5c6be324756aea3f1f2e0808eea3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/12a64c63cffd5c6be324756aea3f1f2e0808eea3"}],"sha":"b7dd784525547ad178e11c94ff47d2d6322848f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/b7dd784525547ad178e11c94ff47d2d6322848f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/12a64c63cffd5c6be324756aea3f1f2e0808eea3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T13:01:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T13:01:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"ci: enforce migration hygiene and an up/down/up round-trip\n\nNothing in CI looked at backend/migrations/. Every guarantee about that\ndirectory was manual and per-PR, which meant the next migration inherited\nno protection.\n\nStatic checks (backend/migrations_static_test.go, no database, so they run\nin every job including the Docker one): three-digit lower_snake_case\nfilenames, an up and a down for every version, no version claimed twice,\nversions contiguous from 001, and both directions readable through the same\niofs driver main.go uses. That last one reproduces the incident in #31\ndirectly — the crash there was a failed *down* read.\n\nRound trip (backend/migrations_roundtrip_test.go, needs Postgres): walk the\nset up one version at a time recording the schema at each step, walk back\ndown comparing each step against what was recorded, then re-apply the whole\nset and compare against the first pass. Stepping rather than dropping\nstraight to zero is what makes an incomplete down detectable: 001''s down\ndrops the tables outright, so a later down that forgets to remove a column\nstill ends at an empty schema and still re-ups identically. Verified by\ngutting 006''s down — the step-wise check names the column and its CHECK\nconstraint, the whole-cycle version passes.\n\nThe snapshot compares columns, constraints, indexes, triggers, functions,\nextensions and sequences in schema public, rendered via pg_get_*def.\n\nFixes 001_initial.down.sql, which the new check caught: it dropped the\nentries table (taking its trigger) but never the update_updated_at()\nfunction the trigger called, so the function survived a full rollback.\n\nAlso extracts newMigrator() from runMigrations() so tests can drive\nmigrations without the startup-only log.Fatalf handling — same shape as the\nearlier validateJWTSecret() refactor. No behaviour change.\n\nCI runs the round trip in the existing Backend Tests (Go) job against a\npostgres:16-alpine service. The test never migrates the database it is\npointed at; it creates a uniquely-named throwaway and drops it afterwards.\nWithout a URL it skips, so make test-backend and the Docker test image stay\ngreen offline — and CI sets MIGRATE_TEST_REQUIRE_DB=1 so broken wiring\nfails the build rather than silently skipping the check.\n\nCloses #32\nRefs #31\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012b2hMdAMobgbEjdMECJoS2","tree":{"sha":"5793a833da53c23e128ed0a75f49fb675ed19075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/trees/5793a833da53c23e128ed0a75f49fb675ed19075"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/commits/12a64c63cffd5c6be324756aea3f1f2e0808eea3","verification":{"payload":"tree 5793a833da53c23e128ed0a75f49fb675ed19075\nparent 54ca5f0143cdce1e48f8163874ee41c036ca1c7f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785157298 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785157298 +0000\n\nci: enforce migration hygiene and an up/down/up round-trip\n\nNothing in CI looked at backend/migrations/. Every guarantee about that\ndirectory was manual and per-PR, which meant the next migration inherited\nno protection.\n\nStatic checks (backend/migrations_static_test.go, no database, so they run\nin every job including the Docker one): three-digit lower_snake_case\nfilenames, an up and a down for every version, no version claimed twice,\nversions contiguous from 001, and both directions readable through the same\niofs driver main.go uses. That last one reproduces the incident in #31\ndirectly — the crash there was a failed *down* read.\n\nRound trip (backend/migrations_roundtrip_test.go, needs Postgres): walk the\nset up one version at a time recording the schema at each step, walk back\ndown comparing each step against what was recorded, then re-apply the whole\nset and compare against the first pass. Stepping rather than dropping\nstraight to zero is what makes an incomplete down detectable: 001''s down\ndrops the tables outright, so a later down that forgets to remove a column\nstill ends at an empty schema and still re-ups identically. Verified by\ngutting 006''s down — the step-wise check names the column and its CHECK\nconstraint, the whole-cycle version passes.\n\nThe snapshot compares columns, constraints, indexes, triggers, functions,\nextensions and sequences in schema public, rendered via pg_get_*def.\n\nFixes 001_initial.down.sql, which the new check caught: it dropped the\nentries table (taking its trigger) but never the update_updated_at()\nfunction the trigger called, so the function survived a full rollback.\n\nAlso extracts newMigrator() from runMigrations() so tests can drive\nmigrations without the startup-only log.Fatalf handling — same shape as the\nearlier validateJWTSecret() refactor. No behaviour change.\n\nCI runs the round trip in the existing Backend Tests (Go) job against a\npostgres:16-alpine service. The test never migrates the database it is\npointed at; it creates a uniquely-named throwaway and drops it afterwards.\nWithout a URL it skips, so make test-backend and the Docker test image stay\ngreen offline — and CI sets MIGRATE_TEST_REQUIRE_DB=1 so broken wiring\nfails the build rather than silently skipping the check.\n\nCloses #32\nRefs #31\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012b2hMdAMobgbEjdMECJoS2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDwVbVR1\nfxKjuRnUpQyNeDFi1I1M7rkr0+c7zXQCKr9UGh99GBXxaSkmUvgTFC16HZYmRChzsrb+64Wbs4gV\nQwM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T13:01:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/12a64c63cffd5c6be324756aea3f1f2e0808eea3","node_id":"C