te_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/38cce7d4c42cc46c275bfe429594da380e751f89","node_id":"C_kwDOSkir09oAKDM4Y2NlN2Q0YzQyY2M0NmMyNzViZmU0Mjk1OTRkYTM4MGU3NTFmODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/3853a02aac7a84ecc4481aab4d09c370e8948305","sha":"3853a02aac7a84ecc4481aab4d09c370e8948305","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/3853a02aac7a84ecc4481aab4d09c370e8948305"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/77ef8a16c4c468f28de9110e1e854cd82508dd72","sha":"77ef8a16c4c468f28de9110e1e854cd82508dd72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/77ef8a16c4c468f28de9110e1e854cd82508dd72"}],"sha":"38cce7d4c42cc46c275bfe429594da380e751f89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/38cce7d4c42cc46c275bfe429594da380e751f89"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/77ef8a16c4c468f28de9110e1e854cd82508dd72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T11:46:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T11:46:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: refuse a restore whose dump is ahead of the embedded migrations\n\nBackups include schema_migrations, so restoring a dump taken on a branch with a\nnewer migration sets the database to that version. The API embeds migrations at\ncompile time, so it then finds the database ahead of itself and refuses to start,\ncrash-looping with:\n\n    Migration failed: no migration found for version 7: read down for version 7\n    migrations: file does not exist\n\nnginx has no backend at that point, so every /api call returns a 502 HTML page\nand the login form fails on JSON.parse. This is not hypothetical — it happened on\na real deployment: a version-7 backup restored onto a build embedding 001-006.\n\n`restore` already printed \"confirm it matches this branch: make db-version\" after\nthe fact. That is the wrong end of the operation: by the time you can run it, the\nold database is gone.\n\nThe pre-flight now reads the dump''s own schema_migrations version and compares it\nagainst backend/migrations/, which is what the binary embeds. A dump that is ahead\nis refused before anything is dropped, with a message naming both versions and the\nerror it would otherwise produce. Restoring an older dump is unaffected — that\ndirection is safe, the API just applies the missing migrations.\n\nThe version is read from the COPY block, so it works for both formats: plain .sql\ndirectly, custom archives via `pg_restore -f -`. This re-reads a custom archive a\nsecond time after the integrity pass, which is only noticeable on very large dumps.\n\nFORCE=1 now also downgrades the version check to a warning, for scripted use or\nwhen you are about to check out the branch carrying that migration. It still does\nnot bypass the truncation check.\n\nVerified against a real PostgreSQL 16 with the actual recipes: version-7 dumps in\nboth formats refused with the API never stopped and the database untouched;\nFORCE=1 proceeds; version-6 and version-4 dumps restore normally; the truncation\nguards still fire.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017tCq6wpbxaq4nKJep4kqr6","tree":{"sha":"95908803ac89daca92de93bca0af205355911b6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/trees/95908803ac89daca92de93bca0af205355911b6e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/commits/77ef8a16c4c468f28de9110e1e854cd82508dd72","verification":{"payload":"tree 95908803ac89daca92de93bca0af205355911b6e\nparent 2000da71838e7728a864672083b04c8ac4dd8b9d\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785152762 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785152762 +0000\n\nfix: refuse a restore whose dump is ahead of the embedded migrations\n\nBackups include schema_migrations, so restoring a dump taken on a branch with a\nnewer migration sets the database to that version. The API embeds migrations at\ncompile time, so it then finds the database ahead of itself and refuses to start,\ncrash-looping with:\n\n    Migration failed: no migration found for version 7: read down for version 7\n    migrations: file does not exist\n\nnginx has no backend at that point, so every /api call returns a 502 HTML page\nand the login form fails on JSON.parse. This is not hypothetical — it happened on\na real deployment: a version-7 backup restored onto a build embedding 001-006.\n\n`restore` already printed \"confirm it matches this branch: make db-version\" after\nthe fact. That is the wrong end of the operation: by the time you can run it, the\nold database is gone.\n\nThe pre-flight now reads the dump''s own schema_migrations version and compares it\nagainst backend/migrations/, which is what the binary embeds. A dump that is ahead\nis refused before anything is dropped, with a message naming both versions and the\nerror it would otherwise produce. Restoring an older dump is unaffected — that\ndirection is safe, the API just applies the missing migrations.\n\nThe version is read from the COPY block, so it works for both formats: plain .sql\ndirectly, custom archives via `pg_restore -f -`. This re-reads a custom archive a\nsecond time after the integrity pass, which is only noticeable on very large dumps.\n\nFORCE=1 now also downgrades the version check to a warning, for scripted use or\nwhen you are about to check out the branch carrying that migration. It still does\nnot bypass the truncation check.\n\nVerified against a real PostgreSQL 16 with the actual recipes: version-7 dumps in\nboth formats refused with the API never stopped and the database untouched;\nFORCE=1 proceeds; version-6 and version-4 dumps restore normally; the truncation\nguards still fire.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017tCq6wpbxaq4nKJep4kqr6\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNMyoHuk\nX6Gd0if4dqbFNZh338swQDdFmfKhggAIgniuOYzIQPjx9CyAo6Sbg35xaD+sj6JC7HjU9SdSok8g\nHQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T11:46:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/77ef8a16c4c468f28de9110e1e854cd82508dd72","node_id":"C_kwDOSkir09oAKDc3ZWY4YTE2YzRjNDY4ZjI4ZGU5MTEwZTFlODU0Y2Q4MjUwOGRkNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/2000da71838e7728a864672083b04c8ac4dd8b9d","sha":"2000da71838e7728a864672083b04c8ac4dd8b9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/2000da71838e7728a864672083b04c8ac4dd8b9d"}],"sha":"77ef8a16c4c468f28de9110e1e854cd82508dd72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/77ef8a16c4c468f28de9110e1e854cd82508dd72"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/436414?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar","id":436414,"login":"Vertikar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNjQxNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ve