ttps://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/3853a02aac7a84ecc4481aab4d09c370e8948305","node_id":"C_kwDOSkir09oAKDM4NTNhMDJhYWM3YTg0ZWNjNDQ4MWFhYjRkMDljMzcwZTg5NDgzMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/6e48e4d73bde120007d7f18bc75d8e546d847082","sha":"6e48e4d73bde120007d7f18bc75d8e546d847082","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/6e48e4d73bde120007d7f18bc75d8e546d847082"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c","sha":"a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c"}],"sha":"3853a02aac7a84ecc4481aab4d09c370e8948305","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/3853a02aac7a84ecc4481aab4d09c370e8948305"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/3c3d06d7c78cfd169eebb1068d4dcd4e313665a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T07:09:23Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T07:09:23Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: validate backups before restore drops the database\n\nPR #33 made `make restore` drop schema public and load the dump in a single\ntransaction with ON_ERROR_STOP=1, and documented the result as \"either fully\nsucceeds or leaves the existing data untouched\". That holds for a dump that\nraises a SQL error. It does not hold for a truncated one.\n\nON_ERROR_STOP only fires on an error. Truncation is not an error: psql reaches\nend-of-file, exits 0, and --single-transaction COMMITS. Running the checklist''s\nown corrupt-dump test against a real PostgreSQL 16:\n\n  head -50 backup.sql > broken.sql   -> exit 0, \"Restored from broken.sql.\",\n                                        database left with an empty schema\n  head -200 backup.sql               -> exit 0, commits users=0 entries=0\n                                        budgets=1 with no FKs or indexes\n\nThe second is a silent half-restore, the exact failure this change set out to\nremove, and both are worse than the original bug because the schema is dropped\nfirst.\n\nFix it in two parts:\n\n- `backup` writes pg_dump custom format (-Fc). A custom archive is\n  self-describing, so truncation is a hard read error rather than a silent EOF.\n- `restore` reads and validates the whole file BEFORE dropping anything, and\n  still accepts both formats so existing .sql backups stay restorable. Custom\n  archives are decoded with `pg_restore -f /dev/null`; `pg_restore -l` is not\n  sufficient, as it reads only the table of contents and passes on an archive\n  whose data blocks are gone. Plain .sql is gated on pg_dump''s end-of-dump\n  trailer.\n\nAlso:\n\n- `db-version` no longer reports every failure as an empty database. It checks\n  to_regclass first, so a stopped container or bad credentials surfaces its own\n  error and a non-zero exit instead of \"the database is empty\".\n- `restore` restarts the API from a trap, so Ctrl-C mid-restore no longer\n  leaves it stopped.\n- `FORCE=1` skips the confirmation delay so `restore` can be scripted.\n- Ignore *.dump; retag the PR #33 follow-ups in TODO.md from #pr-31 to #pr-33.\n\nREADME and CLAUDE.md now state what is actually guaranteed: a validated backup\nloads atomically, and an incomplete one is refused before the database is\ntouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017tCq6wpbxaq4nKJep4kqr6","tree":{"sha":"9052e15b551fa1845dc46f2f086d596b6574115c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/trees/9052e15b551fa1845dc46f2f086d596b6574115c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/commits/3c3d06d7c78cfd169eebb1068d4dcd4e313665a7","verification":{"payload":"tree 9052e15b551fa1845dc46f2f086d596b6574115c\nparent a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785136163 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785136163 +0000\n\nfix: validate backups before restore drops the database\n\nPR #33 made `make restore` drop schema public and load the dump in a single\ntransaction with ON_ERROR_STOP=1, and documented the result as \"either fully\nsucceeds or leaves the existing data untouched\". That holds for a dump that\nraises a SQL error. It does not hold for a truncated one.\n\nON_ERROR_STOP only fires on an error. Truncation is not an error: psql reaches\nend-of-file, exits 0, and --single-transaction COMMITS. Running the checklist''s\nown corrupt-dump test against a real PostgreSQL 16:\n\n  head -50 backup.sql > broken.sql   -> exit 0, \"Restored from broken.sql.\",\n                                        database left with an empty schema\n  head -200 backup.sql               -> exit 0, commits users=0 entries=0\n                                        budgets=1 with no FKs or indexes\n\nThe second is a silent half-restore, the exact failure this change set out to\nremove, and both are worse than the original bug because the schema is dropped\nfirst.\n\nFix it in two parts:\n\n- `backup` writes pg_dump custom format (-Fc). A custom archive is\n  self-describing, so truncation is a hard read error rather than a silent EOF.\n- `restore` reads and validates the whole file BEFORE dropping anything, and\n  still accepts both formats so existing .sql backups stay restorable. Custom\n  archives are decoded with `pg_restore -f /dev/null`; `pg_restore -l` is not\n  sufficient, as it reads only the table of contents and passes on an archive\n  whose data blocks are gone. Plain .sql is gated on pg_dump''s end-of-dump\n  trailer.\n\nAlso:\n\n- `db-version` no longer reports every failure as an empty database. It checks\n  to_regclass first, so a stopped container or bad credentials surfaces its own\n  error and a non-zero exit instead of \"the database is empty\".\n- `restore` restarts the API from a trap, so Ctrl-C mid-restore no longer\n  leaves it stopped.\n- `FORCE=1` skips the confirmation delay so `restore` can be scripted.\n- Ignore *.dump; retag the PR #33 follow-ups in TODO.md from #pr-31 to #pr-33.\n\nREADME and CLAUDE.md now state what is actually guaranteed: a validated backup\nloads atomically, and an incomplete one is refused before the database is\ntouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017tCq6wpbxaq4nKJep4kqr6\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCUQ+wbP\nAZoEwkeHXUGy5b1PpUm9aJaLQwKB3/LViDVfjvI+kkpiNRnzQs3oBVx8ylzmry3DkzGlTOPDp8SH\n1QQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T07:09:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/3c3d06d7c78cfd169eebb1068d4dcd4e313665a7","node_id":"C_kwDOSkir09oAKDNjM2QwNmQ3Yzc4Y2ZkMTY5ZWViYjEwNjhkNGRjZDRlMzEzNjY1YTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c","sha":"a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c"}],"sha":"3c3d06d7c78cfd169eebb1068d4dcd4e313665a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/3c3d06d7c78cfd169eebb1068d4dcd4e313665a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T05:52:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T05:52:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: make restore replace the database atomically instead of half-restoring\n\n`make restore` piped a plain pg_dump into a database that still had all its\nobjects, with no ON_ERROR_STOP. psql ignored every failure and kept going, so\nthe restore \"succeeded\" with data missing.\n\nThe silent loss came from ordering: pg_dump emits COPY alphabetically\n(budgets, categories, entries, ... users). On an empty database that is safe\nbecause constraints are added after the data, but against a populated database\nthe foreign keys already existed, so budgets and entries were rejected against\nthe *old* users rows and were never restored.\n\nrestore now drops schema public and loads the dump in a single transaction with\nON_ERROR_STOP=1, so it either fully succeeds or leaves the existing data\nuntouched. The API container is stopped for the duration so nothing writes\nmid-restore, and restarted afterwards on both the success and failure paths.\n\nbackup now dumps with --clean --if-exists --no-owner --no-privileges.\n\nAlso:\n\n- Add `make db-version` (issue 1, item 3) — the first diagnostic for migration\n  version drift, which a restore can now reintroduce because dumps include\n  schema_migrations.\n- Resolve the database user and name from the db container''s own POSTGRES_USER\n  and POSTGRES_DB rather than the hardcoded `finance` literals, so they cannot\n  drift from what docker-compose passed in from .env. Overridable per\n  invocation with DB_USER= / DB_NAME=.\n- Document the branch-switching hazard in README and CLAUDE.md (issue 1,\n  item 6), including that backups carry a schema version.\n- Refresh the stale migrations table in the README (it stopped at 002).\n- Ignore .worktrees/.\n\nNo production code changes; Makefile and docs only.","tree":{"sha":"90771cb5418ec3d2d0c3e3695e4feb8d8cd9873d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/trees/90771cb5418ec3d2d0c3e3695e4feb8d8cd9873d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/commits/a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c","node_id":"C_kwDOSkir09oAKGEzY2UxYmUyZmExODU5MTY2NjY4MDBiZTEzMzZmMjZmYjJkZTk5MGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/6e48e4d73bde120007d7f18bc75d8e546d847082","sha":"6e48e4d73bde120007d7f18bc75d8e546d847082","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/6e48e4d73bde120007d7f18bc75d8e546d847082"}],"sha":"a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/a3ce1be2fa185916666800be1336f26fb2de990c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/bed4bdcc0a62f9deecc4928cdef80453f62916f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T03:53:55Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T03:53:55Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: explain the mismatch when a bank statement is dropped into the entries importer\n\nThe entries importer requires name, amount, type, frequency, category and\nnext_due. A bank statement shares exactly one of those (amount) and has no\nfrequency column at all — it cannot have one, since frequency is inferred\nfrom many transactions rather than stated per row.\n\nDropping a statement therefore produced \"Missing required columns: name,\ntype, frequency, category, next_due\", which reads as though the file were\nmalformed rather than taken to the wrong door, with no indication that a\ntransaction importer exists.\n\nWhen the dropped file''s headers look like a statement, the modal now shows\none muted line beneath the error explaining that this importer sets up\nrecurring entries and that raw transactions are handled separately. The\nwording deliberately does not link anywhere: the transaction import has no\nUI entry point yet, and pointing at a button that does not exist would be\nworse than saying nothing. A follow-up upgrades it to a real link once that\nscreen lands.\n\nDetection lives in utils.js as a pure helper and requires two signal columns\nrather than one, so an entries CSV carrying an incidental `balance` column\nis not mistaken for a statement.\n\nFrontend only; no backend or API changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CEVhDCXBcM9b3CoXo63qL2","tree":{"sha":"5438c7f128445bd753c47f26c9e5fd826cf70498","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/trees/5438c7f128445bd753c47f26c9e5fd826cf70498"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/commits/bed4bdcc0a62f9deecc4928cdef80453f62916f6","verification":{"payload":"tree 5438c7f128445bd753c47f26c9e5fd826cf70498\nparent 6e48e4d73bde120007d7f18bc75d8e546d847082\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785124435 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785124435 +0000\n\nfix: explain the mismatch when a bank statement is dropped into the entries importer\n\nThe entries importer requires name, amount, type, frequency, category and\nnext_due. A bank statement shares exactly one of those (amount) and has no\nfrequency column at all — it cannot have one, since frequency is inferred\nfrom many transactions rather than stated per row.\n\nDropping a statement therefore produced \"Missing required columns: name,\ntype, frequency, category, next_due\", which reads as though the file were\nmalformed rather than taken to the wrong door, with no indication that a\ntransaction importer exists.\n\nWhen the dropped file''s headers look like a statement, the modal now shows\none muted line beneath the error explaining that this importer sets up\nrecurring entries and that raw transactions are handled separately. The\nwording deliberately does not link anywhere: the transaction import has no\nUI entry point yet, and pointing at a button that does not exist would be\nworse than saying nothing. A follow-up upgrades it to a real link once that\nscreen lands.\n\nDetection lives in utils.js as a pure helper and requires two signal columns\nrather than one, so an entries CSV carrying an incidental `balance` column\nis not mistaken for a statement.\n\nFrontend only; no backend or API changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CEVhDCXBcM9b3CoXo63qL2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB6eYUOO\n1IDya8ROwnS3t5QUj8qRbsqfdCC31z8JB7hBLnWvv/gZYEk4u3eikMpCCJOBFIJVqE/57BTBGFUf\niQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T03:54:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/bed4bdcc0a62f9deecc4928cdef80453f62916f6","node_id":"C_kwDOSkir09oAKGJlZDRiZGNjMGE2MmY5ZGVlY2M0OTI4Y2RlZjgwNDUzZjYyOTE2ZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/6e48e4d73bde120007d7f18bc75d8e546d847082","sha":"6e48e4d73bde120007d7f18bc75d8e546d847082","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/6e48e4d73bde120007d7f18bc75d8e546d847082"}],"sha":"bed4bdcc0a62f9deecc4928cdef80453f62916f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/bed4bdcc0a62f9deecc4928cdef80453f62916f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/436414?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar","id":436414,"login":"Vertikar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNjQxNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vertikar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"h