b-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/8a3adfc11ab77024dc9a20369b54cfd6280caf80","node_id":"C_kwDOSkir09oAKDhhM2FkZmMxMWFiNzcwMjRkYzlhMjAzNjliNTRjZmQ2MjgwY2FmODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/4f4e47ac9d1ad8a1deb2ec731862cd781d9ec1ba","sha":"4f4e47ac9d1ad8a1deb2ec731862cd781d9ec1ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/4f4e47ac9d1ad8a1deb2ec731862cd781d9ec1ba"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/7851b94885d05d2b813ed88c2cc06602c5cb935f","sha":"7851b94885d05d2b813ed88c2cc06602c5cb935f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/7851b94885d05d2b813ed88c2cc06602c5cb935f"}],"sha":"8a3adfc11ab77024dc9a20369b54cfd6280caf80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/8a3adfc11ab77024dc9a20369b54cfd6280caf80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/663014eff80ab09d1a2aff9ad9f531503fca9932/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T11:01:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T11:01:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix payment-frequency date edge cases (month-end, leap day, timezone)\n\nRecurring-payment date stepping had several latent bugs that surfaced in\nthe Cash Flow and Pay Cycle views:\n\n- Month-end overflow: a monthly/quarterly/biannual/yearly bill due on the\n  29th-31st used setMonth(), which overflows (\"Feb 31\" -> Mar 3), skipping\n  short months and permanently drifting the due day.\n- Leap-day drift: a yearly bill due Feb 29 drifted to Mar 1 forever.\n- UTC-vs-local parsing: buildCashFlow parsed nextDue as UTC midnight while\n  getExpensesDueInCycle used local, so displayed dates could shift a day.\n\nFixes:\n- addFreq/prevFreq now take an optional anchorDay and clamp month/year steps\n  to the target month''s length via shiftMonths(), so a bill due the 31st\n  lands Jan 31, Feb 28, Mar 31, Apr 30 with no skipping or drift.\n- Standardize all nextDue parsing on local midnight (parseLocal) and format\n  due strings with toDateStr() instead of toISOString().\n- Extract a shared occurrencesInWindow() generator used by buildCashFlow and\n  getExpensesDueInCycle; App.js now imports buildCashFlow instead of keeping\n  duplicate copies of addFreq/toMonthly and an inline cash-flow loop.\n- Add sumActualForMonth() and surface a calendar-accurate \"this month\" figure\n  on the Overview, so heavy months (3 fortnightly / 5 weekly payments) show\n  the real total alongside the averaged monthly-equivalent.\n\nAdds unit tests for end-of-month anchoring, leap-day yearly, the 3-fortnightly\nJuly case, and sumActualForMonth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MRK8nwCCKzZg9o8TAvtDxM","tree":{"sha":"df18dc799aff195db7e37c440734b1a117198bdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/trees/df18dc799aff195db7e37c440734b1a117198bdd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/git/commits/663014eff80ab09d1a2aff9ad9f531503fca9932","verification":{"payload":"tree df18dc799aff195db7e37c440734b1a117198bdd\nparent 4f4e47ac9d1ad8a1deb2ec731862cd781d9ec1ba\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782039700 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1782039700 +0000\n\nFix payment-frequency date edge cases (month-end, leap day, timezone)\n\nRecurring-payment date stepping had several latent bugs that surfaced in\nthe Cash Flow and Pay Cycle views:\n\n- Month-end overflow: a monthly/quarterly/biannual/yearly bill due on the\n  29th-31st used setMonth(), which overflows (\"Feb 31\" -> Mar 3), skipping\n  short months and permanently drifting the due day.\n- Leap-day drift: a yearly bill due Feb 29 drifted to Mar 1 forever.\n- UTC-vs-local parsing: buildCashFlow parsed nextDue as UTC midnight while\n  getExpensesDueInCycle used local, so displayed dates could shift a day.\n\nFixes:\n- addFreq/prevFreq now take an optional anchorDay and clamp month/year steps\n  to the target month''s length via shiftMonths(), so a bill due the 31st\n  lands Jan 31, Feb 28, Mar 31, Apr 30 with no skipping or drift.\n- Standardize all nextDue parsing on local midnight (parseLocal) and format\n  due strings with toDateStr() instead of toISOString().\n- Extract a shared occurrencesInWindow() generator used by buildCashFlow and\n  getExpensesDueInCycle; App.js now imports buildCashFlow instead of keeping\n  duplicate copies of addFreq/toMonthly and an inline cash-flow loop.\n- Add sumActualForMonth() and surface a calendar-accurate \"this month\" figure\n  on the Overview, so heavy months (3 fortnightly / 5 weekly payments) show\n  the real total alongside the averaged monthly-equivalent.\n\nAdds unit tests for end-of-month anchoring, leap-day yearly, the 3-fortnightly\nJuly case, and sumActualForMonth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MRK8nwCCKzZg9o8TAvtDxM\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK1aVg+9\nZQW9fgRjbwEtJK2MHPoCo9/Sv9mPqyaH7gjQVPUDtapS73lxeJmCMJ+uUt3uOapxLCDBzCkb7uxa\nuwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-21T11:01:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/663014eff80ab09d1a2aff9ad9f531503fca9932","node_id":"C_kwDOSkir09oAKDY2MzAxNGVmZjgwYWIwOWQxYTJhZmY5YWQ5ZjUzMTUwM2ZjYTk5MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commit/4f4e47ac9d1ad8a1deb2ec731862cd781d9ec1ba","sha":"4f4e47ac9d1ad8a1deb2ec731862cd781d9ec1ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/4f4e47ac9d1ad8a1deb2ec731862cd781d9ec1ba"}],"sha":"663014eff80ab09d1a2aff9ad9f531503fca9932","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vertikar/finance-fullstack/commits/663014eff80ab09d1a2aff9ad9f5315