rivacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-doctor/commit/84ce412f4cdb225d9ac72ed789e8a5d943964a68","node_id":"C_kwDOSlNf4NoAKDg0Y2U0MTJmNGNkYjIyNWQ5YWM3MmVkNzg5ZThhNWQ5NDM5NjRhNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-doctor/commit/3f347811f59a32376005f8bbedfdec3e78da0038","sha":"3f347811f59a32376005f8bbedfdec3e78da0038","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-doctor/commits/3f347811f59a32376005f8bbedfdec3e78da0038"}],"sha":"84ce412f4cdb225d9ac72ed789e8a5d943964a68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-doctor/commits/84ce412f4cdb225d9ac72ed789e8a5d943964a68"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-doctor/commits/3f347811f59a32376005f8bbedfdec3e78da0038/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T21:44:19Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T21:44:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(notifications): republish doctor probe warn/fail to SignalK (#50)\n\n* feat(notifications): republish doctor probe warn/fail to SignalK\n\nThe doctor engine''s health probes (including the new timezone-drift check)\nwere only visible in the doctor console — they never reached SignalK, so\nalarm panels (KIP, etc.) couldn''t surface them. The engine is read-only\ntoward signalk-server by design, so the plugin is the right place to bridge.\n\nPoll GET /api/probes on an interval and republish each warn/fail probe as a\nnotification under notifications.doctor.<probe-id>: warn -> state:warn\n(visual), fail -> state:alarm (visual+sound). When a probe recovers (or goes\nok/unknown/absent) its notification is cleared with state:normal, and stop()\nclears all still-active ones so nothing latches after shutdown. unknown is\ndeliberately not raised (a couldn''t-measure state that would flap on boot).\n\nA transient engine-unreachable cycle is skipped without clearing existing\nnotifications, so a blip doesn''t spuriously resolve real alarms. Off-switch\nand interval are config (publishNotifications default on, min 10s). The poll\nloop never throws out of start().\n\n* fix(notifications): harden poll lifecycle; env-port; docs\n\nAddress review on the probe-notifications feature:\n\n- Start polling BEFORE the 30s signalk-container wait and outside the\n  manager-missing early return, so notifications work even when\n  signalk-container never loads (they only need the engine''s /api/probes).\n- Guard the poll loop: an in-flight cycle can''t overlap the next (skip\n  while running) or reconcile after stop() (a pollStopped flag checked\n  post-fetch), so a shutdown never re-raises a just-cleared alarm.\n- Clamp a NaN/Infinity interval to the schema default before the floor, so\n  a malformed config can''t turn setInterval into a ~1ms hot loop.\n- Catch reconcile()/handleMessage() throws at the timer boundary (debug\n  log, not an unhandled rejection).\n- Drop probes with an empty id (would emit notifications.doctor.) and\n  cancel non-OK response bodies to free pooled connections.\n- Make the engine port overridable via SIGNALK_DOCTOR_ENGINE_PORT (also\n  used by the e2e), defaulting to 3004.\n- README: document the feature, config keys, and status→state mapping.\n\ne2e against a real signalk-server 2.30.0 confirmed the round-trip: a warn\nprobe surfaces as notifications.doctor.<id> state=warn, recovery flips it\nto state=normal, and stop() clears it (no latched alarm).\n\n* fix(notifications): poll generation + interval ceiling\n\nTwo lifecycle hardening fixes from review:\n\n- A rapid stop() -> start() reset the shared pollStopped boolean to false\n  while an old fetch was still in flight; that stale cycle could pass its\n  stopped-check, reconcile against the already-cleared notifier\n  (re-raising alarms), and clobber the new run''s pollInFlight. Replace the\n  boolean with a per-run generation counter; a cycle whose generation no\n  longer matches is stale and skips reconcile.\n- Clamp the poll interval to a 3600s ceiling (schema maximum + runtime\n  cap) so a huge notificationIntervalSeconds can''t overflow\n  intervalS*1000 past Node''s 32-bit setInterval limit into a rapid loop.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"2489c2808d1d32346c225a3dc26ff6eadd91a17d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-doctor/git/trees/2489c2808d1d32346c225a3dc26ff6eadd91a17d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-doctor/git/commits/3f347811f59a32376005f8bbedfdec3e78da0038","verification":{"payload":"tree 2489c2808d1d32346c225a3dc26ff6eadd91a17d\nparent 24cc26abca1c8ae9168c0c83a7a464490a8d2c31\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1785102259 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785102259 +1200\n\nfeat(notifications): republish doctor probe warn/fail to SignalK (#50)\n\n* feat(notifications): republish doctor probe warn/fail to SignalK\n\nThe doctor engine''s health probes (including the new timezone-drift check)\nwere only visible in the doctor console — they never reached SignalK, so\nalarm panels (KIP, etc.) couldn''t surface them. The engine is read-only\ntoward signalk-server by design, so the plugin is the right place to bridge.\n\nPoll GET /api/probes on an interval and republish each warn/fail probe as a\nnotification under notifications.doctor.<probe-id>: warn -> state:warn\n(visual), fail -> state:alarm (visual+sound). When a probe recovers (or goes\nok/unknown/absent) its notification is cleared with state:normal, and stop()\nclears all still-active ones so nothing latches after shutdown. unknown is\ndeliberately not raised (a couldn''t-measure state that would flap on boot).\n\nA transient engine-unreachable cycle is skipped without clearing existing\nnotifications, so a blip doesn''t spuriously resolve real alarms. Off-switch\nand interval are config (publishNotifications default on, min 10s). The poll\nloop never throws out of start().\n\n* fix(notifications): harden poll lifecycle; env-port; docs\n\nAddress review on the probe-notifications feature:\n\n- Start polling BEFORE the 30s signalk-container wait and outside the\n  manager-missing early return, so notifications work even when\n  signalk-container never loads (they only need the engine''s /api/probes).\n- Guard the poll loop: an in-flight cycle can''t overlap the next (skip\n  while running) or reconcile after stop() (a pollStopped flag checked\n  post-fetch), so a shutdown never re-raises a just-cleared alarm.\n- Clamp a NaN/Infinity interval to the schema default before the floor, so\n  a malformed config can''t turn setInterval into a ~1ms hot loop.\n- Catch reconcile()/handleMessage() throws at the timer boundary (debug\n  log, not an unhandled rejection).\n- Drop probes with an empty id (would emit notifications.doctor.) and\n  cancel non-OK response bodies to free pooled connections.\n- Make the engine port overridable via SIGNALK_DOCTOR_ENGINE_PORT (also\n  used by the e2e), defaulting to 3004.\n- README: document the feature, config keys, and status→state mapping.\n\ne2e against a real signalk-server 2.30.0 confirmed the round-trip: a warn\nprobe surfaces as notifications.doctor.<id> state=warn, recovery flips it\nto state=normal, and stop() clears it (no latched alarm).\n\n* fix(notifications): poll generation + interval ceiling\n\nTwo lifecycle hardening fixes from review:\n\n- A rapid stop() -> start() reset the shared pollStopped boolean to false\n  while an old fetch was still in flight; that stale cycle could pass its\n  stopped-check, reconcile against the already-cleared notifier\n  (re-raising alarms), and clobber the new run''s pollInFlight. Replace the\n  boolean with a per-run generation counter; a cycle whose generation no\n  longer matches is stale and skips reconcile.\n- Clamp the poll interval to a 3600s ceiling (schema maximum + runtime\n  cap) so a huge notificationIntervalSeconds can''t overflow\n  intervalS*1000 past Node''s 32-bit setInterval limit into a rapid loop.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZn+zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsLMQAI4fOevQtTz6nzNVDXg8DDFl\nSJ7HWKF/tNtV3Tz+fS1P