octor/commits/0dfa7c76b74a1065b3661fb5396643d4edaab41a"}],"sha":"ebc5543598682637592ef65ed8914c0ac8aa881a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-doctor/commits/ebc5543598682637592ef65ed8914c0ac8aa881a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-doctor/commits/0dfa7c76b74a1065b3661fb5396643d4edaab41a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-13T21:38:11Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-13T21:38:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(health): retry engine probe and flag slow as I/O (#42)\n\nThe startup health probe fired a single 5s fetch and, on any miss, set a red\n\"not reachable\" plugin error. On a busy or microSD-bound host the engine can\nanswer its own /api/health in 3-4s, so a healthy service got reported as down.\nRetry twice (5s per attempt, ~2s apart) before erroring, and when the engine\nanswers but slowly (>1.5s) set a status (not an error) noting likely disk I/O\nand the SSD fix — SignalK''s plugin API has no warning tier, so it''s a green\nstatus; the Doctor Console''s storage-type probe carries the SD-card detail.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"1bae8dc27e2d984867249920f9de5bb17472f077","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-doctor/git/trees/1bae8dc27e2d984867249920f9de5bb17472f077"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-doctor/git/commits/0dfa7c76b74a1065b3661fb5396643d4edaab41a","verification":{"payload":"tree 1bae8dc27e2d984867249920f9de5bb17472f077\nparent e427851d2098741bdb0e1bfcf503a1419e1899cd\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1781386691 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781386691 +1200\n\nfix(health): retry engine probe and flag slow as I/O (#42)\n\nThe startup health probe fired a single 5s fetch and, on any miss, set a red\n\"not reachable\" plugin error. On a busy or microSD-bound host the engine can\nanswer its own /api/health in 3-4s, so a healthy service got reported as down.\nRetry twice (5s per attempt, ~2s apart) before erroring, and when the engine\nanswers but slowly (>1.5s) set a status (not an error) noting likely disk I/O\nand the SSD fix — SignalK''s plugin API has no warning tier, so it''s a green\nstatus; the Doctor Console''s storage-type probe carries the SD-card detail.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLc3DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAURQQAJ5+XcpYRK9+yluDm89czUl7\nUo+V2oxSVFgh7R2CPyrbhQY1ADuzOGCYpCRB1llvcLbswBd9J/XmZUT56Hr/pb2M\n4Jv0tMSi3Pg77kNdj51UxMoC5ZNnP2JtAoKKjwUQ3faCnrg4IHKiCpTMfwxm+T8B\ncZ5X1q9Y76HR1pLDn9f9DekFfh3OA+pz/02JkOb8x7nIpZEK8DcGSgQYndTUuxqK\nsZSzROHZ05YH9A2fThB0JjKtuHR0RlsTOzh+PiyObGEzZAlV+GHpHm8e+yturkpO\n1lQBrPZw0qjl+racQinO1ghogomy6aOw4ID+B3++EJ09nMgT2a1Lt+CfLjSnK83A\njAzL/PKdXGXJM8XhCuaPqRzseI7jcNFh+o5BnbQcpqUBeVcDMQTouqsi3Aip33Uc\nhlmQ7xBNctEy1J6yyYxhtWq5V+ZwyqwO2vcjYeK7Wcz9wZS8TeUA0IbImsykAEMc\ngmb6pt/IY8AHr3KZXMRorOwZMBMNc