rianstanca1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adrianstanca1","id":192421473,"login":"adrianstanca1","node_id":"U_kgDOC3geYQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adrianstanca1/cortexx/commits/8ad5ea518a6accc5c9f9291c9c81e6255e135c31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:25:52Z","email":"adrian.stanca1@gmail.com","name":"adrian stanca"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:25:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(llm): keep Ollama models resident to skip reload on idle requests (#285)\n\n* perf(llm): keep Ollama models resident to skip reload on idle requests\n\nOllama unloads a model 5 minutes after its last request (its own default).\nEvery AI request following a quiet period therefore paid a full model load\nbefore generating a single token. Measured on this host (16 cores,\nrotational disk): load_duration of 3349-5437ms on top of ~5-7s inference,\nso a post-idle request took 11.6s where a warm one takes 4.9s.\n\nSend keep_alive with both Ollama request bodies so the configured model\nstays in memory between requests. 30m covers the gap within a working\nsession while bounding residency to 2.5GB (qwen3:4b) + 1.7GB (moondream)\nagainst ~27GB free. Overridable per-deployment via OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE.\n\nThe OpenAI-compatible llama-server branch is left alone — it has no\nkeep_alive field.\n\nVerified against the live model: warm-path load_duration drops from 3349ms\nto 1ms; first call after a full unload still pays the load as expected.\n\n* fix(llm): omit keep_alive for Ollama default instead of sending \"0\"\n\nDocumented OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=\"0\" as restoring Ollama''s default, but Ollama\nreads \"0\" as ''unload immediately'' — so an operator following that comment\nwould have reloaded the model on every request, re-introducing the exact\nlatency this setting exists to remove.\n\nAn empty or ''default'' value now omits the field entirely, which is what\nactually defers to Ollama''s server default (5m). Flagged by both CodeRabbit\nand the Codex reviewer on #285.\n\n* test(llm): pin keepAliveField semantics, especially the \"0\" trap\n\nRegression cover for the defect flagged by CodeRabbit and the Codex reviewer\non #285: keep_alive:\"0\" makes Ollama unload after every response rather than\nfalling back to its 5m default, which would reinstate the ~3.3s load on every\nrequest. Asserts that empty/''default'' omits the field, that \"0\" passes through\nverbatim, and that spreading the helper doesn''t clobber sibling body fields.\n\nFull suite: 600/600 pass.\n\n* fix(llm): emit numeric keep_alive for bare numeric values\n\nP2 from the Codex reviewer on #285: OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=-1 was advertised as the\npermanent-residency value but sent as the JSON string \"-1\". Ollama parses\nstring durations with Go''s time.ParseDuration, which rejects a unitless value,\nso every Ollama-backed chat returned HTTP 400. Verified against a live Ollama:\n\n    keep_alive: \"-1\"  -> 400 time: missing unit in duration \"-1\"\n    keep_alive: -1     -> 200\n    keep_alive: \"-1m\" -> 200\n\nBare numerics are now emitted as JSON numbers; duration strings are unaffected.\nAlso corrects the doc comment to advertise \"-1m\" as the string form.\n\ntsc clean; full suite 601/601 pass.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Hermes Agent <agent@hermes.local>\nCo-authored-by: adrian stanca <192421473+adrianstanca1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"654953d789aa6a7a96e6c8410c6ce85108c122c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adrianstanca1/cortexx/git/trees/654953d789aa6a7a96e6c8410c6ce85108c122c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adrianstanca1/cortexx/git/commits/8ad5ea518a6accc5c9f9291c9c81e6255e135c31","verification":{"payload":"tree 654953d789aa6a7a96e6c8410c6ce85108c122c0\nparent 4a9fbd5cce2eba26f7d9e2ea7582ff3195f67ec7\nauthor adrian stanca <adrian.stanca1@gmail.com> 1791289552 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791289552 +0100\n\nperf(llm): keep Ollama models resident to skip reload on idle requests (#285)\n\n* perf(llm): keep Ollama models resident to skip reload on idle requests\n\nOllama unloads a model 5 minutes after its last request (its own default).\nEvery AI request following a quiet period therefore paid a full model load\nbefore generating a single token. Measured on this host (16 cores,\nrotational disk): load_duration of 3349-5437ms on top of ~5-7s inference,\nso a post-idle request took 11.6s where a warm one takes 4.9s.\n\nSend keep_alive with both Ollama request bodies so the configured model\nstays in memory between requests. 30m covers the gap within a working\nsession while bounding residency to 2.5GB (qwen3:4b) + 1.7GB (moondream)\nagainst ~27GB free. Overridable per-deployment via OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE.\n\nThe OpenAI-compatible llama-server branch is left alone — it has no\nkeep_alive field.\n\nVerified against the live model: warm-path load_duration drops from 3349ms\nto 1ms; first call after a full unload still pays the load as expected.\n\n* fix(llm): omit keep_alive for Ollama default instead of sending \"0\"\n\nDocumented OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=\"0\" as restoring Ollama''s default, but Ollama\nreads \"0\" as ''unload immediately'' — so an operator following that comment\nwould have reloaded the model on every request, re-introducing the exact\nlatency this setting exists to remove.\n\nAn empty or ''default'' value now omits the field entirely, which is what\nactually defers to Ollama''s server default (5m). Flagged by both CodeRabbit\nand the Codex reviewer on #285.\n\n* test(llm): pin keepAliveField semantics, especially the \"0\" trap\n\nRegression cover for the defect flagged by CodeRabbit and the Codex reviewer\non #285: keep_alive:\"0\" makes Ollama unload after every response rather than\nfalling back to its 5m default, which would reinstate the ~3.3s load on every\nrequest. Asserts that empty/''default'' omits the field, that \"0\" passes through\nverbatim, and that spreading the helper doesn''t clobber sibling body fields.\n\nFull suite: 600/600 pass.\n\n* fix(llm): emit numeric keep_alive for bare numeric values\n\nP2 from the Codex reviewer on #285: OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=-1 was advertised as the\npermanent-residency value but sent as the JSON string \"-1\". Ollama parses\nstring durations with Go''s time.ParseDuration, which rejects a unitless value,\nso every Ollama-backed chat returned HTTP 400. Verified against a live Ollama:\n\n    keep_alive: \"-1\"  -> 400 time: missing unit in duration \"-1\"\n    keep_alive: -1     -> 200\n    keep_alive: \"-1m\" -> 200\n\nBare numerics are now emitted as JSON numbers; duration strings are unaffected.\nAlso corrects the doc comment to advertise \"-1m\" as the string form.\n\ntsc clean; full suite 601/601 pass.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Hermes Agent <agent@hermes.local>\nCo-authored-by: adrian stanca <192421473+adrianstanca1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxOjQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnfwQAJWkC0aQuyf5wm3vL9XsW4+Q\nrGsdkoVCN3lVfzgayCBpQVEtmvsj8wDzDLG2qBQjh14BQ3EoG9NqTomzkK/KrXN2\nApuGaawdXMIAyU0atDWfZTlIN9Hk6HIhnKc05o1kWoebT/IklZ1s0ageRVY/kcDu\nvb1/5MoSVZuUJeeaMcftTPNDEB6fhaV00BUEkLPAm0ao+rdYFreyKwlKcmZhHhUI\ntMcb14GK0MAaKEZbDB6In8TiNyiN4LYaaMNKDD+BhYcYUol15BQe3Pkw5OylyrX1\np/ZEWz4Hy7NoEyoitMJExWlIhcRVufemp6bhevouud9XUlMs7e+kMWXUS9yS0m/v\nam3ASeIPhy8YuUjBZsOQ6zTJyaBrDm/We1mtkIgL8