nca1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adrianstanca1","id":192421473,"login":"adrianstanca1","node_id":"U_kgDOC3geYQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adrianstanca1/cortexx/commits/3c6a44a1e9807f8a23132134018d1a97d1f1137c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:37:46Z","email":"adrian.stanca1@gmail.com","name":"adrian stanca"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:37:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Retire cortexbuildpro.com; canonical Apple associations; browser gateway (#280)\n\n* feat: port browser gateway + admin console from cortexbuild-pro\n\nBrings over the unique files from the sibling cortexbuild-pro repo rather\nthan merging it wholesale. The two repos share 188 files, 154 of which have\ndiverged (docker-compose.yml alone differs by 159 lines, Caddyfile by 67), so\na merge would clobber current production config and trigger deploy workflows.\nThis ports only what cortexx does not already have.\n\nAdded:\n- browser-gateway/ — Puppeteer + Socket.IO agent control plane. Holds a\n  per-agent command queue in Redis and exposes an HTML dashboard. Serves\n  /browser-gateway/* through Caddy; no host port is published.\n- admin/ — vanilla-JS admin console (login, overview, users, projects,\n  workspaces, billing, system, shared api/ui/core helpers).\n- lib/{presence.js,presence-ui.jsx,screens-auth.jsx,screens-diagnostics.jsx,\n  side-menu.jsx} + their compiled dist/ outputs.\n\nWiring:\n- Caddyfile: /api/agent/* and /browser-gateway/* reverse proxies. Both are\n  declared before the /api/* catch-all and the @blocked deny handler, which\n  is required — Caddy matches top-to-bottom, so the catch-all would otherwise\n  swallow /api/agent/* and it could never respond. browser-gateway is added\n  to the file_server hide list so the static source copy is not served.\n- docker-compose.yml: new browser-gateway service, plus the redis:7-alpine\n  it depends on (there was no redis service before).\n\nHardening applied during the port (the source was written for a single-operator\nlaptop, not a public edge):\n- JWT_SECRET fails closed. No default, no fallback. Missing secret aborts\n  `docker compose config` instead of booting with a guessable key.\n- CORS is same-origin rather than a wildcard.\n- JSON body limit 50mb -> 2mb.\n- REDIS_HOST/REDIS_PORT are env-configurable, and .env.example documents\n  BROWSER_GATEWAY_JWT_SECRET, REDIS_HOST, ALLOWED_ORIGIN.\n- Dockerfile: `npm ci --production` -> `npm ci` (the flag is deprecated in\n  npm 9+ and npm ci already installs exactly what the lockfile pins), plus\n  the Chromium/alpine shared libraries Puppeteer needs. Without them the\n  container starts but every browser launch fails.\n\nFixed on port:\n- server.js did not parse. The inline <script> in the res.send(`...`)\n  dashboard contained nested template literals, which closed the outer\n  literal early and made the HTML parse as JavaScript. Rewritten to string\n  concatenation so the block contains no backticks.\n- dist/ staleness: build-dist.js --check is enforced in CI and auto-discovers\n  lib/*.jsx, so the 5 ported modules needed their compiled outputs committed\n  alongside the sources.\n\nAll five sensitive gateway routes (/api/browser/start, /api/browser/action,\n/api/agents/status, /api/agent/command, /api/system-state) require a JWT.\nOnly /health and the dashboard shell are unauthenticated, and the shell\ncontains no secrets.\n\n* fix: satisfy cortexx app-integrity and React compiler gates\n\nPorted UI used bare React.createElement(''button'', {...}) with no type\nproperty, which cortexx''s own scripts/audit-app-integrity.mjs rejects.\nAdded type: ''button'' to all 10 occurrences (screens-auth, screens-diagnostics,\nside-menu). None of these files contain a <form> or onSubmit handler, so\nnone of the buttons are genuine submits — without an explicit type they\nwould have defaulted to type=\"submit\" had they ever been nested in a form.\n\nadmin-app.jsx assigned to location.hash directly, which the React 19\ncompiler ruleset (react-hooks/immutability, an error in Next''s\ncore-web-vitals config) rejects as mutating a value owned outside the\ncomponent. Switched to history.pushState, which also makes Back/Forward work,\nand added a popstate listener alongside the existing hashchange one since\nthe two fire together for hash navigation.\n\ndist/ recompiled to match. Verified locally: audit:app 0 findings,\nlint clean, lint:a11y clean at --max-warnings 0, tsc --noEmit clean,\n563 unit tests pass, nav-registry pass, prisma drift guard pass,\nlint:smells pass, docker compose config parses, gateway server.js parses.\n\n* feat: harden private browser gateway control plane\n\n* chore: remove validation symlink\n\n* fix: enforce browser gateway egress policy\n\n* Retire cortexbuildpro.com; fix studio ingress port and .well-known 307s\n\nThree defects, all verified against live production.\n\n1. studio.cortexbuildpro.tech proxied to the wrong application.\n   The Caddyfile routed that hostname to 127.0.0.1:3000, which is\n   faceless-video-studio-1 (\"Cortex Video Studio — Local Long Videos\").\n   Viral Shorts Studio publishes 127.0.0.1:3010 (PORT=3010). The subdomain\n   also has no DNS A record, so the block was dead config asserting an\n   ingress that would have published the wrong product.\n\n2. /.well-known/security.txt and the AASA file returned 307 -> /login.\n   Two independent causes: proxy.ts did not list them as public paths, and\n   the files lived in a repo-root .well-known/ directory which Next.js\n   never serves (only public/ is). This broke the Universal Links\n   requirement documented in docs/IOS_CI.md.\n\n3. 139 references to the retired cortexbuildpro.com remained across 55\n   files, including user-visible support/sales/press addresses in\n   /help and /pricing, the monitoring agent''s health URL, iOS applinks\n   entitlements, and the CI E2E fixture emails.\n\nReference classes deliberately left as .com, because rewriting them would\nbe wrong (see ops/sweep-com-to-tech.mjs):\n  - server/db/migrations/ — applied seeds; rewriting changes their checksum\n  - test/canonical-domain-mobile-auth.test.js — the guard test''s own needle\n  - docs/reviews/, docs/patches/ — the historical retirement record\n\nVerification:\n  npm test              570 pass, 0 fail\n  npm run test:integration  67 pass, 0 fail, 0 skipped\n                       (previously 12 skipped for want of TEST_DATABASE_URL;\n                        ran against the local cortexx-task-progress-e2e-pg\n                        container on 127.0.0.1:55441)\n  npm run lint          clean\n  test/well-known-public.test.js  4 pass, and a negative control confirms\n                       the guard fails when public/.well-known is removed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Serve verified Apple associations from runtime configuration\n\n* Repoint seeded support_email off retired cortexbuildpro.com\n\nMigration 006 seeded platform_settings.general.support_email with\nsupport@cortexbuildpro.com. That domain is retired and its registrar\ndelegation SERVFAILs, so the address is undeliverable -- and it is served\nby GET/PUT /admin/settings, so operators can still read and re-save it.\n\n006 is applied history and stays untouched; this is a forward fix, guarded\non the exact legacy value so a hand-corrected address is never clobbered.\n\nVerified against Postgres 16: repoints the legacy row, preserves an\noperator-corrected row, and is idempotent (second run affects 0 rows).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: adrian stanca <192421473+adrianstanca1@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hermes Agent <agent@cortexbuildpro.tech>","tree":{"sha":"96d37eb54988e05af83a66659d3f591e6b2d60ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adrianstanca1/cortexx/git/trees/96d37eb54988e05af83a66659d3f591e6b2d60ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adrianstanca1/cortexx/git/commits/3c6a44a1e9807f8a23132134018d1a97d1f1137c","verification":{"payload":"tree 96d37eb54988e05af83a66659d3f591e6b2d60ce\nparent 2bb32484125c961be1b91035ad1cc27cfda5ee94\nauthor adrian stanca <adrian.stanca1@gmail.com> 1791157066 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791157066 +0100\n\nRetire cortexbuildpro.com; canonical Apple associations; browser gateway (#280)\n\n* feat: port browser gateway + admin console from cortexbuild-pro\n\nBrings over the unique files from the sibling cortexbuild-pro repo rather\nthan merging it wholesale. The two repos share 188 files, 154 of which have\ndiverged (docker-compose.yml alone differs by 159 lines, Caddyfile by 67), so\na merge would clobber current production config and trigger deploy workflows.\nThis ports only what cortexx does not already have.\n\nAdded:\n- browser-gateway/ — Puppeteer + Socket.IO agent control plane. Holds a\n  per-agent command queue in Redis and exposes an HTML dashboard. Serves\n  /browser-gateway/* through Caddy; no host port is published.\n- admin/ — vanilla-JS admin console (login, overview, users, projects,\n  workspaces, billing, system, shared api/ui/core helpers).\n- lib/{presence.js,presence-ui.jsx,screens-auth.jsx,screens-diagnostics.jsx,\n  side-menu.jsx} + their compiled dist/ outputs.\n\nWiring:\n- Caddyfile: /api/agent/* and /browser-gateway/* reverse proxies. Both are\n  declared before the /api/* catch-all and the @blocked deny handler, which\n  is required — Caddy matches top-to-bottom, so the catch-all would otherwise\n  swallow /api/agent/* and it could never respond. browser-gateway is added\n  to the file_server hide list so the static source copy is not served.\n- docker-compose.yml: new browser-gateway service, plus the redis:7-alpine\n  it depends on (there was no redis service before).\n\nHardening applied during the port (the source was written for a single-operator\nlaptop, not a public edge):\n- JWT_SECRET fails closed. No default, no fallback. Missing secret aborts\n  `docker compose config` instead of booting with a guessable key.\n- CORS is same-origin rather than a wildcard.\n- JSON body limit 50mb -> 2mb.\n- REDIS_HOST/REDIS_PORT are env-configurable, and .env.example documents\n  BROWSER_GATEWAY_JWT_SECRET, REDIS_HOST, ALLOWED_ORIGIN.\n- Dockerfile: `npm ci --production` -> `npm ci` (the flag is deprecated in\n  npm 9+ and npm ci already installs exactly what the lockfile pins), plus\n  the Chromium/alpine shared libraries Puppeteer needs. Without them the\n  container starts but every browser launch fails.\n\nFixed on port:\n- server.js did not parse. The inline <script> in the res.send(`...`)\n  dashboard contained nested template literals, which closed the outer\n  literal early and made the HTML parse as JavaScript. Rewritten to string\n  concatenation so the block contains no backticks.\n- dist/ staleness: build-dist.js --check is enforced in CI and auto-discovers\n  lib/*.jsx, so the 5 ported modules needed their compiled outputs committed\n  alongside the sources.\n\nAll five sensitive gateway routes (/api/browser/start, /api/browser/action,\n/api/agents/status, /api/agent/command, /api/system-state) require a JWT.\nOnly /health and the dashboard shell are unauthenticated, and the shell\ncontains no secrets.\n\n* fix: satisfy cortexx app-integrity and React compiler gates\n\nPorted UI used bare React.createElement(''button'', {...}) with no type\nproperty, which cortexx''s own scripts/audit-app-integrity.mjs rejects.\nAdded type: ''button'' to all 10 occurrences (screens-auth, screens-diagnostics,\nside-menu). None of these files contain a <form> or onSubmit handler, so\nnone of the buttons are genuine submits — without an explicit type they\nwould have defaulted to type=\"submit\" had they ever been nested in a form.\n\nadmin-app.jsx assigned to location.hash directly, which the React 19\ncompiler ruleset (react-hooks/immutability, an error in Next''s\ncore-web-vitals config) rejects as mutating a value owned outside the\ncomponent. Switched to history.pushState, which also makes Back/Forward work,\nand added a popstate listener alongside the existing hashchange one since\nthe two fire together for hash navigation.\n\ndist/ recompiled to match. Verified locally: audit:app 0 findings,\nlint clean, lint:a11y clean at --max-warnings 0, tsc --noEmit clean,\n563 unit tests pass, nav-registry pass, prisma drift guard pass,\nlint:smells pass, docker compose config parses, gateway server.js parses.\n\n* feat: harden private browser gateway control plane\n\n* chore: remove validation symlink\n\n* fix: enforce browser gateway egress policy\n\n* Retire cortexbuildpro.com; fix studio ingress port and .well-known 307s\n\nThree defects, all verified against live production.\n\n1. studio.cortexbuildpro.tech proxied to the wrong application.\n   The Caddyfile routed that hostname to 127.0.0.1:3000, which is\n   faceless-video-studio-1 (\"Cortex Video Studio — Local Long Videos\").\n   Viral Shorts Studio publishes 127.0.0.1:3010 (PORT=3010). The subdomain\n   also has no DNS A record, so the block was dead config asserting an\n   ingress that would have published the wrong product.\n\n2. /.well-known/security.txt and the AASA file returned 307 -> /login.\n   Two independent causes: proxy.ts did not list them as public paths, and\n   the files lived in a repo-root .well-known/ directory which Next.js\n   never serves (only public/ is). This broke the Universal Links\n   requirement documented in docs/IOS_CI.md.\n\n3. 139 references to the retired cortexbuildpro.com remained across 55\n   files, including user-visible support/sales/press addresses in\n   /help and /pricing, the monitoring agent''s health URL, iOS applinks\n   entitlements, and the CI E2E fixture emails.\n\nReference classes deliberately left as .com, because rewriting them would\nbe wrong (see ops/sweep-com-to-tech.mjs):\n  - server/db/migrations/ — applied seeds; rewriting changes their checksum\n  - test/canonical-domain-mobile-auth.test.js — the guard test''s own needle\n  - docs/reviews/, docs/patches/ — the historical retirement record\n\nVerification:\n  npm test              570 pass, 0 fail\n  npm run test:integration  67 pass, 0 fail, 0 skipped\n                       (previously 12 skipped for want of TEST_DATABASE_URL;\n                        ran against the local cortexx-task-progress-e2e-pg\n                        container on 127.0.0.1:55441)\n  npm run lint          clean\n  test/well-known-public.test.js  4 pass, and a negative control confirms\n                       the guard fails when public/.well-known is removed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Serve verified Apple associations from runtime configuration\n\n* Repoint seeded support_email off retired cortexbuildpro.com\n\nMigration 006 seeded platform_settings.general.support_email with\nsupport@cortexbuildpro.com. That domain is retired and its registrar\ndelegation SERVFAILs, so the address is undeliverable -- and it is served\nby GET/PUT /admin/settings, so operators can still read and re-save it.\n\n006 is applied history and stays untouched; this is a forward fix, guarded\non the exact legacy value so a hand-corrected address is never clobbered.\n\nVerified against Postgres 16: repoints the legacy row, preserves an\noperator-corrected row, and is idempotent (second run affects 0 rows).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: adrian stanca <192421473+adrianstanca1@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hermes Agent <agent@cortexbuildpro.tech>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwuNKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6pYQAIUcw4oYfDlOCjLJU6bMVnno\n9gYAHLKZAbegcM4H/krygWP58j1TwDYETz701zmjde13XNwaMGPFhtWWqiGz5qsp\n96UiDPjOjLyf7iaEtzxp+Vlk6d+g1kPOhQV96fqpdnz8rJ0LKmhoRHH4YnrmI82f\n+Wyicn9DvoSeeMIh0Nmzwz45ne/gHLdjlEWJgj2u8Udq6azdlX9AcHEeN5i4AF9s\nUF/2u52bxT6BKXRodnssxohxSVlO1m10qXo6CfKT/N0nnSrtFROv2MFKLKKQouTe\nUxr239uVqAWnkCuy2cWC5HwuHlXGmEbbm71Zt+56vwePY6hrFu6PELEq5SJ7ZXcu\nZhBMIzNttVE/vIk1H6lkhrxyet6ViU2zEgv6vGq+yFXGqp7maTMyXZP58JMsftLT\nDAqlUzGybRZ8tj0n3uM8lSZKAQCX11FD9ywryG9YzDZHBuVXZy82oohI4VPgjLg1\nzM4DVvatGwjGKCJ2F71kG6V8aUmJkHzQMcr1BlPM6vdLSpIl1jD08Ypgka5TWk1x\nyXrNV0XXMYVP455GmvFSEnc1gIYFTN4XXfsYao6qVMUl4sau8lNkghESf9IK4gyN\nMSpklB+jCOoQ+rbephJ39Tr/H4/0GbqiGKqtZvfcgp0AB+skoWBWeghLa/GHh/kJ\nHJhhU+9YCC8pYO6/gTrn\n=x3fo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T23:37:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.githu