ublishes 127.0.0.1:3010 (PORT=3010). The subdomain\n   also has no DNS A record, so the block was dead config asserting an\n   ingress that would have published the wrong product.\n\n2. /.well-known/security.txt and the AASA file returned 307 -> /login.\n   Two independent causes: proxy.ts did not list them as public paths, and\n   the files lived in a repo-root .well-known/ directory which Next.js\n   never serves (only public/ is). This broke the Universal Links\n   requirement documented in docs/IOS_CI.md.\n\n3. 139 references to the retired cortexbuildpro.com remained across 55\n   files, including user-visible support/sales/press addresses in\n   /help and /pricing, the monitoring agent''s health URL, iOS applinks\n   entitlements, and the CI E2E fixture emails.\n\nReference classes deliberately left as .com, because rewriting them would\nbe wrong (see ops/sweep-com-to-tech.mjs):\n  - server/db/migrations/ — applied seeds; rewriting changes their checksum\n  - test/canonical-domain-mobile-auth.test.js — the guard test''s own needle\n  - docs/reviews/, docs/patches/ — the historical retirement record\n\nVerification:\n  npm test              570 pass, 0 fail\n  npm run test:integration  67 pass, 0 fail, 0 skipped\n                       (previously 12 skipped for want of TEST_DATABASE_URL;\n                        ran against the local cortexx-task-progress-e2e-pg\n                        container on 127.0.0.1:55441)\n  npm run lint          clean\n  test/well-known-public.test.js  4 pass, and a negative control confirms\n                       the guard fails when public/.well-known is removed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Serve verified Apple associations from runtime configuration\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: adrian stanca <192421473+adrianstanca1@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFc