ithub.com/adrianstanca1/cortexx/commit/a83f9fc83073a32476ce4a47f49faf0bd1286a4e","sha":"a83f9fc83073a32476ce4a47f49faf0bd1286a4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adrianstanca1/cortexx/commits/a83f9fc83073a32476ce4a47f49faf0bd1286a4e"}],"sha":"f166351663e589e91206b60fbd6c81c44c81bcfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adrianstanca1/cortexx/commits/f166351663e589e91206b60fbd6c81c44c81bcfe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192421473?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/adrianstanca1","id":192421473,"login":"adrianstanca1","node_id":"U_kgDOC3geYQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrianstanca1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adrianstanca1/cortexx/commits/a83f9fc83073a32476ce4a47f49faf0bd1286a4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:48:00Z","email":"adrian.stanca1@gmail.com","name":"adrian stanca"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:48:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add hardened private browser gateway (#276)\n\n* feat: port browser gateway + admin console from cortexbuild-pro\n\nBrings over the unique files from the sibling cortexbuild-pro repo rather\nthan merging it wholesale. The two repos share 188 files, 154 of which have\ndiverged (docker-compose.yml alone differs by 159 lines, Caddyfile by 67), so\na merge would clobber current production config and trigger deploy workflows.\nThis ports only what cortexx does not already have.\n\nAdded:\n- browser-gateway/ — Puppeteer + Socket.IO agent control plane. Holds a\n  per-agent command queue in Redis and exposes an HTML dashboard. Serves\n  /browser-gateway/* through Caddy; no host port is published.\n- admin/ — vanilla-JS admin console (login, overview, users, projects,\n  workspaces, billing, system, shared api/ui/core helpers).\n- lib/{presence.js,presence-ui.jsx,screens-auth.jsx,screens-diagnostics.jsx,\n  side-menu.jsx} + their compiled dist/ outputs.\n\nWiring:\n- Caddyfile: /api/agent/* and /browser-gateway/* reverse proxies. Both are\n  declared before the /api/* catch-all and the @blocked deny handler, which\n  is required — Caddy matches top-to-bottom, so the catch-all would otherwise\n  swallow /api/agent/* and it could never respond. browser-gateway is added\n  to the file_server hide list so the static source copy is not served.\n- docker-compose.yml: new browser-gateway service, plus the redis:7-alpine\n  it depends on (there was no redis service before).\n\nHardening applied during the port (the source was written for a single-operator\nlaptop, not a public edge):\n- JWT_SECRET fails closed. No default, no fallback. Missing secret aborts\n  `docker compose config` instead of booting with a guessable key.\n- CORS is same-origin rather than a wildcard.\n- JSON body limit 50mb -> 2mb.\n- REDIS_HOST/REDIS_PORT are env-configurable, and .env.example documents\n  BROWSER_GATEWAY_JWT_SECRET, REDIS_HOST, ALLOWED_ORIGIN.\n- Dockerfile: `npm ci --production` -> `npm ci` (the flag is deprecated in\n  npm 9+ and npm ci already installs exactly what the lockfile pins), plus\n  the Chromium/alpine shared libraries Puppeteer needs. Without them the\n  container starts but every browser launch fails.\n\nFixed on port:\n- server.js did not parse. The inline <script> in the res.send(`...`)\n  dashboard contained nested template literals, which closed the outer\n  literal early and made the HTML parse as JavaScript. Rewritten to string\n  concatenation so the block contains no backticks.\n- dist/ staleness: build-dist.js --check is enforced in CI and auto-discovers\n  lib/*.jsx, so the 5 ported modules needed their compiled outputs committed\n  alongside the sources.\n\nAll five sensitive gateway routes (/api/browser/start, /api/browser/action,\n/api/agents/status, /api/agent/command, /api/system-state) require a JWT.\nOnly /health and the dashboard shell are unauthenticated, and the shell\ncontains no secrets.\n\n* fix: satisfy cortexx app-integrity and React compiler gates\n\nPorted UI used bare React.createElement(''button'', {...}) with no type\nproperty, which cortexx''s own scripts/audit-app-integrity.mjs rejects.\nAdded type: ''button'' to all 10 occurrences (screens-auth, screens-diagnostics,\nside-menu). None of these files contain a <form> or onSubmit handler, so\nnone of the buttons are genuine submits — without an explicit type they\nwould have defaulted to type=\"submit\" had they ever been nested in a form.\n\nadmin-app.jsx assigned to location.hash directly, which the React 19\ncompiler ruleset (react-hooks/immutability, an error in Next''s\ncore-web-vitals config) rejects as mutating a value owned outside the\ncomponent. Switched to history.pushState, which also makes Back/Forward work,\nand added a popstate listener alongside the existing hashchange one since\nthe two fire together for hash navigation.\n\ndist/ recompiled to match. Verified locally: audit:app 0 findings,\nlint clean, lint:a11y clean at --max-warnings 0, tsc --noEmit clean,\n563 unit tests pass, nav-registry pass, prisma drift guard pass,\nlint:smells pass, docker compose config parses, gateway server.js parses.\n\n* feat: harden private browser gateway control plane\n\n* chore: remove validation symlink\n\n* fix: enforce browser gateway egress policy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: adrian stanca <192421473+adrianstanca1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a86ba6cddb7fcad3ec6471bbcfb94c6faa1f8555","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adrianstanca1/cortexx/git/trees/a86ba6cddb7fcad3ec6471bbcfb94c6faa1f8555"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adrianstanca1/cortexx/git/commits/a83f9fc83073a32476ce4a47f49faf0bd1286a4e","verification":{"payload":"tree a86ba6cddb7fcad3ec6471bbcfb94c6faa1f8555\nparent fe282ae2ab027d672b63cc1707330267e05f2011\nauthor adrian stanca <adrian.stanca1@gmail.com> 1791107280 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791107280 +0000\n\nAdd hardened private browser gateway (#276)\n\n* feat: port browser gateway + admin console from cortexbuild-pro\n\nBrings over the unique files from the sibling cortexbuild-pro repo rather\nthan merging it wholesale. The two repos share 188 files, 154 of which have\ndiverged (docker-compose.yml alone differs by 159 lines, Caddyfile by 67), so\na merge would clobber current production config and trigger deploy workflows.\nThis ports only what cortexx does not already have.\n\nAdded:\n- browser-gateway/ — Puppeteer + Socket.IO agent control plane. Holds a\n  per-agent command queue in Redis and exposes an HTML dashboard. Serves\n  /browser-gateway/* through Caddy; no host port is published.\n- admin/ — vanilla-JS admin console (login, overview, users, projects,\n  workspaces, billing, system, shared api/ui/core helpers).\n- lib/{presence.js,presence-ui.jsx,screens-auth.jsx,screens-diagnostics.jsx,\n  side-menu.jsx} + their compiled dist/ outputs.\n\nWiring:\n- Caddyfile: /api/agent/* and /browser-gateway/* reverse proxies. Both are\n  declared before the /api/* catch-all and the @blocked deny handler, which\n  is required — Caddy matches top-to-bottom, so the catch-all would otherwise\n  swallow /api/agent/* and it could never respond. browser-gateway is added\n  to the file_server hide list so the static source copy is not served.\n- docker-compose.yml: new browser-gateway service, plus the redis:7-alpine\n  it depends on (there was no redis service before).\n\nHardening applied during the port (the source was written for a single-operator\nlaptop, not a public edge):\n- JWT_SECRET fails closed. No default, no fallback. Missing secret aborts\n  `docker compose config` instead of booting with a guessable key.\n- CORS is same-origin rather than a wildcard.\n- JSON body limit 50mb -> 2mb.\n- REDIS_HOST/REDIS_PORT are env-configurable, and .env.example documents\n  BROWSER_GATEWAY_JWT_SECRET, REDIS_HOST, ALLOWED_ORIGIN.\n- Dockerfile: `npm ci --production` -> `npm ci` (the flag is deprecated in\n  npm 9+ and npm ci already installs exactly what the lockfile pins), plus\n  the Chromium/alpine shared libraries Puppeteer needs. Without them the\n  container starts but every browser launch fails.\n\nFixed on port:\n- server.js did not parse. The inline <script> in the res.send(`...`)\n  dashboard contained nested template literals, which closed the outer\n  literal early and made the HTML parse as JavaScript. Rewritten to string\n  concatenation so the block contains no backticks.\n- dist/ staleness: build-dist.js --check is enforced in CI and auto-discovers\n  lib/*.jsx, so the 5 ported modules needed their compiled outputs committed\n  alongside the sources.\n\nAll five sensitive gateway routes (/api/browser/start, /api/browser/action,\n/api/agents/status, /api/agent/command, /api/system-state) require a JWT.\nOnly /health and the dashboard shell are unauthenticated, and the shell\ncontains no secrets.\n\n* fix: satisfy cortexx app-integrity and React compiler gates\n\nPorted UI used bare React.createElement(''button'', {...}) with no type\nproperty, which cortexx''s own scripts/audit-app-integrity.mjs rejects.\nAdded type: ''button'' to all 10 occurrences (screens-auth, screens-diagnostics,\nside-menu). None of these files contain a <form> or onSubmit handler, so\nnone of the buttons are genuine submits — without an explicit type they\nwould have defaulted to type=\"submit\" had they ever been nested in a form.\n\nadmin-app.jsx assigned to location.hash directly, which the React 19\ncompiler ruleset (react-hooks/immutability, an error in Next''s\ncore-web-vitals config) rejects as mutating a value owned outside the\ncomponent. Switched to history.pushState, which also makes Back/Forward work,\nand added a popstate listener alongside the existing hashchange one since\nthe two fire together for hash navigation.\n\ndist/ recompiled to match. Verified locally: audit:app 0 findings,\nlint clean, lint:a11y clean at --max-warnings 0, tsc --noEmit clean,\n563 unit tests pass, nav-registry pass, prisma drift guard pass,\nlint:smells pass, docker compose config parses, gateway server.js parses.\n\n* feat: harden private browser gateway control plane\n\n* chore: remove validation symlink\n\n* fix: enforce browser gateway egress policy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: adrian stanca <192421473+adrianstanca1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwiDQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUYwQAJxuAgGDUNfktDd18eF4oucd\nJWnNdOt7q0/edjYrd+ehbgm/tgvAoDLe8X+MOTcs1kJJGnzuQx17ebIHZILfG/PR\nYxwnZdP8B1JZyHf/3ZJJpildPyLgIl/znB/HeTcnco8ZBDNfidbk3JyLTAKsxAXB\ndcftF5DsK3cxqYw+pj2qBsn2JLJsTlyokHQryI3fa13HteZ1G4Ae7hn8lHYriFSK\nNrHBZYVP8AFvF0VR3GcYdSfGTv27KxRooMIq9NCvAvHLtyukrhRcQvMKm9eoQrJM\nlO2Wf2wuofBU2sH1ZS6FKcJSlOmqyCOe3++dss5iHR5Ifv+LjF6lm3X+0b2jeem3\nSRZ0yJQlQycxs66LeXD3KLhVg84CCsE0bE4vnhW+7+wcDILAuIbh8YCeWOXtLf75\nO7RW5WxpeqTXAUyqVELG+CRw/J83bRSYZ+4S6jmuFYmqY2SRsgXSPz/LlFn8MZaY\n2j3iLPyu4ifAl8+mMjI/t5vVmR+mdpun6j9lFnCKBqn/YAK491kb6d09udlfZjRL\n3IxTild5kjo125QVHH69/1tOZHLH5EmGkkzZ6srXhRORuYgaNiNuvn8/+DXL4pqz\njX5vlD55L2Q7Ft56W3drduofQFeTG5k9/4QsE9X7KSjvsjY9k9IOuKoh6lqqb0zg\nQLaP2WI2NIA8j+/RPjd0\n=//kh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T09:48:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":